    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-9",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9 Simplified outline",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-9"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "The following is a simplified outline of this Part:\nThis Part contains the definitions used in this Act.\nThis Part contains provisions to facilitate the conferral of functions\nand powers on the Regulator under State legislation, in order to\nfacilitate a nationally consistent regulatory scheme.\nThis Part contains provisions to enable the concurrent operation of\ncertain State legislation in relation to GMOs, and gives the\ncapacity for this Act to have a more limited operation when\ncorresponding State legislation is in force.\nThis Part also enables the Ministerial Council to issue policy\nprinciples, policy guidelines and codes of practice.\n\n\nInterpretation and operation of Act  Part 2\nDefinitions  Division 2\nSection 10\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024",
      "skos:definition": "The following is a simplified outline of this Part:\nThis Part contains the definitions used in this Act.\nThis Part contains provisions to facilitate the conferral of functions\nand powers on the Regulator under State legislation, in order to\nfacilitate a nationally consistent regulatory scheme.\nThis Part contains provisions to enable the concurrent operation of\ncertain State legislation in relation to GMOs, and gives the\ncapacity for this Act to have a more limited operation when\ncorresponding State legislation is in force.\nThis Part also enables the Ministerial Council to issue policy\nprinciples, policy guidelines and codes of practice.\n\n\nInterpretation and operation of Act  Part 2\nDefinitions  Division 2\nSection 10\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-9-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "37bad6be85b8d6732390d8574e56295970b44644e7511f686f46feab467c3b2d",
      "skos:note": "Part outline"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-9",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9 Simplified outline",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 16,
      "values:originalText": "The following is a simplified outline of this Part:\nThis Part contains the definitions used in this Act.\nThis Part contains provisions to facilitate the conferral of functions\nand powers on the Regulator under State legislation, in order to\nfacilitate a nationally consistent regulatory scheme.\nThis Part contains provisions to enable the concurrent operation of\ncertain State legislation in relation to GMOs, and gives the\ncapacity for this Act to have a more limited operation when\ncorresponding State legislation is in force.\nThis Part also enables the Ministerial Council to issue policy\nprinciples, policy guidelines and codes of practice.\n\n\nInterpretation and operation of Act  Part 2\nDefinitions  Division 2\nSection 10\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-9-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-9"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-10",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 Definitions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-10"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.17",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears:\nAccount means the Gene Technology Account established by\nsection 129.\naccredited organisation means an organisation accredited under\nDivision 3 of Part 7.\naggravated offence has the meaning given by section 38.\nAustralian Health Ethics Committee means the Australian Health\nEthics Committee established under the National Health and\nMedical Research Council Act 1992.\nCommonwealth authority means the following:\n(a) a body corporate established for a public purpose by or under\nan Act;\n(b) a company in which a controlling interest is held by any one\nof the following persons, or by 2 or more of the following\npersons together:\n(i) the Commonwealth;\n(ii) a body covered by paragraph (a);\n(iii) a body covered by either of the above subparagraphs.\nconfidential commercial information means information declared\nby the Regulator to be confidential commercial information under\nsection 185.\ncontainment level, in relation to a facility, means the degree of\nphysical confinement of GMOs provided by the facility, having\nregard to the design of the facility, the equipment located or\ninstalled in the facility and the procedures generally used within\nthe facility.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears:\nAccount means the Gene Technology Account established by\nsection 129.\naccredited organisation means an organisation accredited under\nDivision 3 of Part 7.\naggravated offence has the meaning given by section 38.\nAustralian Health Ethics Committee means the Australian Health\nEthics Committee established under the National Health and\nMedical Research Council Act 1992.\nCommonwealth authority means the following:\n(a) a body corporate established for a public purpose by or under\nan Act;\n(b) a company in which a controlling interest is held by any one\nof the following persons, or by 2 or more of the following\npersons together:\n(i) the Commonwealth;\n(ii) a body covered by paragraph (a);\n(iii) a body covered by either of the above subparagraphs.\nconfidential commercial information means information declared\nby the Regulator to be confidential commercial information under\nsection 185.\ncontainment level, in relation to a facility, means the degree of\nphysical confinement of GMOs provided by the facility, having\nregard to the design of the facility, the equipment located or\ninstalled in the facility and the procedures generally used within\nthe facility.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-10-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-10-logic-descriptionlogic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-10-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0a012794b9662d24b6d622504ea0f8bce1e0779b2dca787e91cb2b83a48e980b",
      "skos:note": "Definitions for the Act"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-10",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10 Definitions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 17,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears:\nAccount means the Gene Technology Account established by\nsection 129.\naccredited organisation means an organisation accredited under\nDivision 3 of Part 7.\naggravated offence has the meaning given by section 38.\nAustralian Health Ethics Committee means the Australian Health\nEthics Committee established under the National Health and\nMedical Research Council Act 1992.\nCommonwealth authority means the following:\n(a) a body corporate established for a public purpose by or under\nan Act;\n(b) a company in which a controlling interest is held by any one\nof the following persons, or by 2 or more of the following\npersons together:\n(i) the Commonwealth;\n(ii) a body covered by paragraph (a);\n(iii) a body covered by either of the above subparagraphs.\nconfidential commercial information means information declared\nby the Regulator to be confidential commercial information under\nsection 185.\ncontainment level, in relation to a facility, means the degree of\nphysical confinement of GMOs provided by the facility, having\nregard to the design of the facility, the equipment located or\ninstalled in the facility and the procedures generally used within\nthe facility."
    },
    {
