    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-14-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "14 Wind-back of reach of Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-14-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to a State (the notifying State) at a particular\ntime if:\n\n\nInterpretation and operation of Act  Part 2\nOperation of Act  Division 3\nSection 15\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(a) a corresponding State law is in force in the notifying State at\nthat time; and\n(b) a wind-back notice in relation to that State is in force at that\ntime.\n(2) This Act applies as a law of the Commonwealth in the notifying\nState with the following modifications:\n(a) this Act applies as if paragraph 13(1)(c) (which deals with\nthe spread of pests and diseases) had not been enacted;\n(b) this Act does not apply to a dealing with a GMO undertaken:\n(i) by a higher education institution or a State agency; or\n(ii) by a person authorised to undertake the dealing by a\nlicence held under the corresponding State law by a\nhigher education institution or a State agency.\n(3) In this section:\nwind-back notice, in relation to a State, means a notice given by\nthe State to the Minister, under the Gene Technology Agreement,\nstating that this section is to apply to the State.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies to a State (the notifying State) at a particular\ntime if:\n\n\nInterpretation and operation of Act  Part 2\nOperation of Act  Division 3\nSection 15\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(a) a corresponding State law is in force in the notifying State at\nthat time; and\n(b) a wind-back notice in relation to that State is in force at that\ntime.\n(2) This Act applies as a law of the Commonwealth in the notifying\nState with the following modifications:\n(a) this Act applies as if paragraph 13(1)(c) (which deals with\nthe spread of pests and diseases) had not been enacted;\n(b) this Act does not apply to a dealing with a GMO undertaken:\n(i) by a higher education institution or a State agency; or\n(ii) by a person authorised to undertake the dealing by a\nlicence held under the corresponding State law by a\nhigher education institution or a State agency.\n(3) In this section:\nwind-back notice, in relation to a State, means a notice given by\nthe State to the Minister, under the Gene Technology Agreement,\nstating that this section is to apply to the State.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-14-2-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-14-2-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-14-2-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9d3f695d96f2f2b8a6f3affb127b912b1b218ee7c6e6e164828c1e40410cab4a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-14-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "14 Wind-back of reach of Act",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 24,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to a State (the notifying State) at a particular\ntime if:\n\n\nInterpretation and operation of Act  Part 2\nOperation of Act  Division 3\nSection 15\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(a) a corresponding State law is in force in the notifying State at\nthat time; and\n(b) a wind-back notice in relation to that State is in force at that\ntime.\n(2) This Act applies as a law of the Commonwealth in the notifying\nState with the following modifications:\n(a) this Act applies as if paragraph 13(1)(c) (which deals with\nthe spread of pests and diseases) had not been enacted;\n(b) this Act does not apply to a dealing with a GMO undertaken:\n(i) by a higher education institution or a State agency; or\n(ii) by a person authorised to undertake the dealing by a\nlicence held under the corresponding State law by a\nhigher education institution or a State agency.\n(3) In this section:\nwind-back notice, in relation to a State, means a notice given by\nthe State to the Minister, under the Gene Technology Agreement,\nstating that this section is to apply to the State."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-14-2-ss-1",
