    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-17",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "17 Conferral of functions on Commonwealth officers and bodies",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-17"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.26",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A corresponding State law may confer functions, powers and\nduties on the following:\n(a) the Regulator or another officer of the Commonwealth;\n(b) a Commonwealth authority;\n(c) the Ethics and Community Committee;\n(e) the Gene Technology Technical Advisory Committee.\n\n\nInterpretation and operation of Act  Part 2\nProvisions to facilitate a nationally consistent scheme  Division 4\nSection 18\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(2) If a function, power or duty is conferred on a person or body under\nsubsection (1), the person or body may perform the function or\nduty or exercise the power, as the case requires.\n(3) If a corresponding State law is expressed to confer on the\nRegulator the power to determine that dealings be included on the\nGMO Register, the Regulator may include the dealings on the\nGMO Register in accordance with the corresponding State law.\n(4) If a corresponding State law is expressed to confer on the\nRegulator the power to vary the GMO Register, the Regulator may\nvary the GMO Register in accordance with the corresponding State\nlaw.\n(5) If a corresponding State law is expressed to confer on the\nRegulator the power to enter information on the Record of GMO\nDealings, the Regulator may enter the information on the Record in\naccordance with the corresponding State law.\n(6) The Regulator may:\n(a) make any notations in the GMO Register that the Regulator\nconsiders necessary to identify entries that relate to dealings\nincluded on the Register as mentioned in subsection (3) or\n(4); and\n(b) make any notations in the Record of GMO Dealings that the\nRegulator considers necessary to identify entries that relate to\ninformation entered on the Record as mentioned in\nsubsection (5).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A corresponding State law may confer functions, powers and\nduties on the following:\n(a) the Regulator or another officer of the Commonwealth;\n(b) a Commonwealth authority;\n(c) the Ethics and Community Committee;\n(e) the Gene Technology Technical Advisory Committee.\n\n\nInterpretation and operation of Act  Part 2\nProvisions to facilitate a nationally consistent scheme  Division 4\nSection 18\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(2) If a function, power or duty is conferred on a person or body under\nsubsection (1), the person or body may perform the function or\nduty or exercise the power, as the case requires.\n(3) If a corresponding State law is expressed to confer on the\nRegulator the power to determine that dealings be included on the\nGMO Register, the Regulator may include the dealings on the\nGMO Register in accordance with the corresponding State law.\n(4) If a corresponding State law is expressed to confer on the\nRegulator the power to vary the GMO Register, the Regulator may\nvary the GMO Register in accordance with the corresponding State\nlaw.\n(5) If a corresponding State law is expressed to confer on the\nRegulator the power to enter information on the Record of GMO\nDealings, the Regulator may enter the information on the Record in\naccordance with the corresponding State law.\n(6) The Regulator may:\n(a) make any notations in the GMO Register that the Regulator\nconsiders necessary to identify entries that relate to dealings\nincluded on the Register as mentioned in subsection (3) or\n(4); and\n(b) make any notations in the Record of GMO Dealings that the\nRegulator considers necessary to identify entries that relate to\ninformation entered on the Record as mentioned in\nsubsection (5).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-17-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-17-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-17-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-17-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-17-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-17-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6a1683e9e790de2e32990bcb72be93cf84598cb1076de127012f3bf0798f9b06"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-17",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "17 Conferral of functions on Commonwealth officers and bodies",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 26,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A corresponding State law may confer functions, powers and\nduties on the following:\n(a) the Regulator or another officer of the Commonwealth;\n(b) a Commonwealth authority;\n(c) the Ethics and Community Committee;\n(e) the Gene Technology Technical Advisory Committee.\n\n\nInterpretation and operation of Act  Part 2\nProvisions to facilitate a nationally consistent scheme  Division 4\nSection 18\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(2) If a function, power or duty is conferred on a person or body under\nsubsection (1), the person or body may perform the function or\nduty or exercise the power, as the case requires.\n(3) If a corresponding State law is expressed to confer on the\nRegulator the power to determine that dealings be included on the\nGMO Register, the Regulator may include the dealings on the\nGMO Register in accordance with the corresponding State law.\n(4) If a corresponding State law is expressed to confer on the\nRegulator the power to vary the GMO Register, the Regulator may\nvary the GMO Register in accordance with the corresponding State\nlaw.\n(5) If a corresponding State law is expressed to confer on the\nRegulator the power to enter information on the Record of GMO\nDealings, the Regulator may enter the information on the Record in\naccordance with the corresponding State law.\n(6) The Regulator may:\n(a) make any notations in the GMO Register that the Regulator\nconsiders necessary to identify entries that relate to dealings\nincluded on the Register as mentioned in subsection (3) or\n(4); and\n(b) make any notations in the Record of GMO Dealings that the\nRegulator considers necessary to identify entries that relate to\ninformation entered on the Record as mentioned in\nsubsection (5)."
    },
