    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-29",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "29 Delegation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-29"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.32",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Regulator may, by instrument in writing, delegate any of the\nRegulator’s powers or functions to any of the following:\n(a) an employee of the Department;\n(b) an employee of another Department or of a Commonwealth\nauthority, if the functions of the other Department or\nCommonwealth authority relate, whether directly or\nindirectly, to GMOs or GM products;\n(c) an officer or employee of a State agency, if the functions of\nthe State agency relate, whether directly or indirectly, to\nGMOs or GM products.\n(2) In exercising powers or functions under a delegation, the delegate\nmust comply with any directions of the Regulator.\n\n\nThe Gene Technology Regulator  Part 3\n\nSection 30\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Regulator may, by instrument in writing, delegate any of the\nRegulator’s powers or functions to any of the following:\n(a) an employee of the Department;\n(b) an employee of another Department or of a Commonwealth\nauthority, if the functions of the other Department or\nCommonwealth authority relate, whether directly or\nindirectly, to GMOs or GM products;\n(c) an officer or employee of a State agency, if the functions of\nthe State agency relate, whether directly or indirectly, to\nGMOs or GM products.\n(2) In exercising powers or functions under a delegation, the delegate\nmust comply with any directions of the Regulator.\n\n\nThe Gene Technology Regulator  Part 3\n\nSection 30\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-29-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-29-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "885f024569088e701ab8433e82fe57accd64a2cb6c58c451517d7fdd104e2472"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-29",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "29 Delegation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 32,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Regulator may, by instrument in writing, delegate any of the\nRegulator’s powers or functions to any of the following:\n(a) an employee of the Department;\n(b) an employee of another Department or of a Commonwealth\nauthority, if the functions of the other Department or\nCommonwealth authority relate, whether directly or\nindirectly, to GMOs or GM products;\n(c) an officer or employee of a State agency, if the functions of\nthe State agency relate, whether directly or indirectly, to\nGMOs or GM products.\n(2) In exercising powers or functions under a delegation, the delegate\nmust comply with any directions of the Regulator.\n\n\nThe Gene Technology Regulator  Part 3\n\nSection 30\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024"
    },
    {
