    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-34",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "34 Person must not breach conditions of a GMO licence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-34"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.37",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The holder of a GMO licence commits an offence if:\n(a) the holder intentionally takes an action or omits to take an\naction; and\n(b) the action or omission contravenes the licence, and the holder\nknows or is reckless as to that fact.\nNote:\nChapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of\ncriminal responsibility.\n(2) A person covered by a GMO licence commits an offence if:\n(a) the person intentionally takes an action or omits to take an\naction; and\n(b) the person has knowledge of the conditions of the licence;\nand\n(c) the action or omission contravenes a condition of the licence,\nand the person knows or is reckless as to that fact.\nNote:\nChapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of\ncriminal responsibility.\n(3) An offence under this section is punishable on conviction by\nwhichever of the following applies:\n(a) in the case of an aggravated offence— imprisonment for\n5 years or 2,000 penalty units;\n(b) in any other case— imprisonment for 2 years or 500 penalty\nunits.\nNote:\nSection 38 defines aggravated offence.\n(4) A person who commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2)\ncommits a separate offence in respect of each day (including the\nday of a conviction for the offence or any later day) on which the\nperson commits the offence.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The holder of a GMO licence commits an offence if:\n(a) the holder intentionally takes an action or omits to take an\naction; and\n(b) the action or omission contravenes the licence, and the holder\nknows or is reckless as to that fact.\nNote:\nChapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of\ncriminal responsibility.\n(2) A person covered by a GMO licence commits an offence if:\n(a) the person intentionally takes an action or omits to take an\naction; and\n(b) the person has knowledge of the conditions of the licence;\nand\n(c) the action or omission contravenes a condition of the licence,\nand the person knows or is reckless as to that fact.\nNote:\nChapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of\ncriminal responsibility.\n(3) An offence under this section is punishable on conviction by\nwhichever of the following applies:\n(a) in the case of an aggravated offence— imprisonment for\n5 years or 2,000 penalty units;\n(b) in any other case— imprisonment for 2 years or 500 penalty\nunits.\nNote:\nSection 38 defines aggravated offence.\n(4) A person who commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2)\ncommits a separate offence in respect of each day (including the\nday of a conviction for the offence or any later day) on which the\nperson commits the offence.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-34-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-34-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-34-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-34-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d9ad428d0bf65741008587c6c8b3506176abfc5d4e4403278bb683461569af68"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-34",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "34 Person must not breach conditions of a GMO licence",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 37,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The holder of a GMO licence commits an offence if:\n(a) the holder intentionally takes an action or omits to take an\naction; and\n(b) the action or omission contravenes the licence, and the holder\nknows or is reckless as to that fact.\nNote:\nChapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of\ncriminal responsibility.\n(2) A person covered by a GMO licence commits an offence if:\n(a) the person intentionally takes an action or omits to take an\naction; and\n(b) the person has knowledge of the conditions of the licence;\nand\n(c) the action or omission contravenes a condition of the licence,\nand the person knows or is reckless as to that fact.\nNote:\nChapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of\ncriminal responsibility.\n(3) An offence under this section is punishable on conviction by\nwhichever of the following applies:\n(a) in the case of an aggravated offence— imprisonment for\n5 years or 2,000 penalty units;\n(b) in any other case— imprisonment for 2 years or 500 penalty\nunits.\nNote:\nSection 38 defines aggravated offence.\n(4) A person who commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2)\ncommits a separate offence in respect of each day (including the\nday of a conviction for the offence or any later day) on which the\nperson commits the offence."
    },
