    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-35a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "35A Person must not breach conditions of emergency dealing",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 38,
      "values:originalText": "determination\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person intentionally takes an action or omits to take an\naction; and\n(b) the person has knowledge of the conditions to which an\nemergency dealing determination is subject; and\n(c) the action or omission contravenes such a condition, and the\nperson knows or is reckless as to that fact.\nNote:\nChapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of\ncriminal responsibility.\n(2) An offence under this section is punishable on conviction by\nwhichever of the following applies:\n\n\nRegulation of dealings with GMOs  Part 4\nDealings with GMOs must be licensed  Division 2\nSection 35B\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(a) in the case of an aggravated offence—imprisonment for\n5 years or 2,000 penalty units;\n(b) in any other case—imprisonment for 2 years or 500 penalty\nunits.\nNote:\nSection 38 defines aggravated offence."
    },
