    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-38-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "38(2) Aggravated offences—significant damage to health or safety of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-38-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.40",
      "values:originalText": "(2) In order to prove an aggravated offence, the prosecution must\nprove that the person who committed the offence:\n(a) intended his or her conduct to cause significant damage to the\nhealth and safety of people or to the environment; or\n(b) was reckless as to whether that conduct would cause\nsignificant damage to the health and safety of people or to the\nenvironment.\n\n\nLicensing system  Part 5\nSimplified outline  Division 1\nSection 39\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024",
      "skos:definition": "(2) In order to prove an aggravated offence, the prosecution must\nprove that the person who committed the offence:\n(a) intended his or her conduct to cause significant damage to the\nhealth and safety of people or to the environment; or\n(b) was reckless as to whether that conduct would cause\nsignificant damage to the health and safety of people or to the\nenvironment.\n\n\nLicensing system  Part 5\nSimplified outline  Division 1\nSection 39\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-38"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
