    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-40",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40 Person may apply for a licence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-40"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.42",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person may apply to the Regulator for a licence authorising\nspecified dealings with one or more specified GMOs by a person\nor persons.\n(2) The application must be in writing, and must contain:\n(a) such information as is prescribed by the regulations (if any);\nand\n(b) such information as is specified in writing by the Regulator.\n(3) The application must specify whether any of the dealings proposed\nto be authorised by the licence would involve the intentional\nrelease of a GMO into the environment.\n(4) The dealings in respect of which a person may apply for a licence\nmay be:\n(a) all dealings with a GMO, or with a specified class of GMOs;\nor\n(b) a specified class of dealings with a GMO, or with a specified\nclass of GMOs; or\n(c) one or more specified dealings with a GMO, or with a\nspecified class of GMOs.\n(5) The applicant may apply for a licence authorising such dealings by:\n(a) a specified person or persons; or\n(b) a specified class of person; or\n(c) all persons.\n(6) The application must be accompanied by the application fee (if\nany) prescribed by the regulations.\n\n\nLicensing system  Part 5\nLicence applications  Division 2\nSection 40A\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person may apply to the Regulator for a licence authorising\nspecified dealings with one or more specified GMOs by a person\nor persons.\n(2) The application must be in writing, and must contain:\n(a) such information as is prescribed by the regulations (if any);\nand\n(b) such information as is specified in writing by the Regulator.\n(3) The application must specify whether any of the dealings proposed\nto be authorised by the licence would involve the intentional\nrelease of a GMO into the environment.\n(4) The dealings in respect of which a person may apply for a licence\nmay be:\n(a) all dealings with a GMO, or with a specified class of GMOs;\nor\n(b) a specified class of dealings with a GMO, or with a specified\nclass of GMOs; or\n(c) one or more specified dealings with a GMO, or with a\nspecified class of GMOs.\n(5) The applicant may apply for a licence authorising such dealings by:\n(a) a specified person or persons; or\n(b) a specified class of person; or\n(c) all persons.\n(6) The application must be accompanied by the application fee (if\nany) prescribed by the regulations.\n\n\nLicensing system  Part 5\nLicence applications  Division 2\nSection 40A\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-40-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-40-ss-2"
