    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-44",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44 Regulator may consult with applicant",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-44"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.44",
      "values:originalText": "Before considering an application in accordance with the\nrequirements of this Part, the Regulator may consult the applicant,\nor another regulatory agency, on any aspect of the application.",
      "skos:definition": "Before considering an application in accordance with the\nrequirements of this Part, the Regulator may consult the applicant,\nor another regulatory agency, on any aspect of the application.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-44-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-44-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6ba2c3dbe0d19dfe012af7b85bab5109f7e8ee8b42599dbda3ba046b8f63ed96",
      "skos:note": "Consultation with applicant or another agency before considering an application."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-44",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44 Regulator may consult with applicant",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 44,
      "values:originalText": "Before considering an application in accordance with the\nrequirements of this Part, the Regulator may consult the applicant,\nor another regulatory agency, on any aspect of the application."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-44-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-44"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-44-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MAY",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Regulator's obligation to consult with applicant.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Regulator must consider application before consulting applicant.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Regulator may consult applicant or another agency."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-45",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45 Regulator must not use certain information in considering licence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-45"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.44",
      "values:originalText": "application\nIf:\n(a) a person (the first person) applies for a GMO licence; and\n\n\nLicensing system  Part 5\nLicence applications  Division 2\nSection 45\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(b) the first person provides information to the Regulator for the\npurposes of the Regulator’s consideration of the application;\nand\n(c) the information is confidential commercial information;\nthe Regulator must not take that information into account for the\npurposes of considering an application by another person for a\nGMO licence, unless the first person has given written consent for\nthe information to be so taken into account.",
      "skos:definition": "application\nIf:\n(a) a person (the first person) applies for a GMO licence; and\n\n\nLicensing system  Part 5\nLicence applications  Division 2\nSection 45\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(b) the first person provides information to the Regulator for the\npurposes of the Regulator’s consideration of the application;\nand\n(c) the information is confidential commercial information;\nthe Regulator must not take that information into account for the\npurposes of considering an application by another person for a\nGMO licence, unless the first person has given written consent for\nthe information to be so taken into account.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-45-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-45-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "370f26e625804e6a6082622fd4bc0f9ba038bb4d2ed41981cfa49ce8f226370b",
      "skos:note": "Regulator must not use confidential commercial information without consent."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-45",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "45 Regulator must not use certain information in considering licence",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 44,
      "values:originalText": "application\nIf:\n(a) a person (the first person) applies for a GMO licence; and\n\n\nLicensing system  Part 5\nLicence applications  Division 2\nSection 45\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(b) the first person provides information to the Regulator for the\npurposes of the Regulator’s consideration of the application;\nand\n(c) the information is confidential commercial information;\nthe Regulator must not take that information into account for the\npurposes of considering an application by another person for a\nGMO licence, unless the first person has given written consent for\nthe information to be so taken into account."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-45-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-45"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-45-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibition of using confidential information",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Regulator must not use the information.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "unless the first person has given written consent."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-46",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "46 Applications to which this Division applies",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-46"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.46",
      "values:originalText": "This Division applies to an application for a GMO licence if the\nRegulator is satisfied that none of the dealings proposed to be\nauthorised by the licence would involve the intentional release of a\nGMO into the environment.",
      "skos:definition": "This Division applies to an application for a GMO licence if the\nRegulator is satisfied that none of the dealings proposed to be\nauthorised by the licence would involve the intentional release of a\nGMO into the environment.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-46-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-46-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fb02b23a4c9a0df24f52d8ef25fde9b8f30a7ba082ffddaff5952fee5ff164fa",
      "skos:note": "Application for GMO licence must not involve intentional release into environment."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-46",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "46 Applications to which this Division applies",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 46,
      "values:originalText": "This Division applies to an application for a GMO licence if the\nRegulator is satisfied that none of the dealings proposed to be\nauthorised by the licence would involve the intentional release of a\nGMO into the environment."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-46-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-46"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-46-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibition",
      "cml:logicSummary": "No intentional release of GMO into environment.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-46a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "46A Division does not apply to an application relating to inadvertent",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-46a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.46",
      "values:originalText": "dealings\nDespite section 46, this Division does not apply to an application\nfor a GMO licence if the Regulator is satisfied that:\n(a) the dealings proposed to be authorised by the licence are\nlimited to one or more of the following for purposes relating\nto disposing of a GMO:\n(i) conducting experiments with the GMO;\n(ii) propagating the GMO;\n(iii) growing, raising or culturing the GMO;\n(iv) transporting the GMO;\n(v) any other dealings to be undertaken for the purposes of,\nor for purposes relating to, disposing of the GMO; and\n(b) the applicant for the licence came into possession of the\nGMO inadvertently.",
      "skos:definition": "dealings\nDespite section 46, this Division does not apply to an application\nfor a GMO licence if the Regulator is satisfied that:\n(a) the dealings proposed to be authorised by the licence are\nlimited to one or more of the following for purposes relating\nto disposing of a GMO:\n(i) conducting experiments with the GMO;\n(ii) propagating the GMO;\n(iii) growing, raising or culturing the GMO;\n(iv) transporting the GMO;\n(v) any other dealings to be undertaken for the purposes of,\nor for purposes relating to, disposing of the GMO; and\n(b) the applicant for the licence came into possession of the\nGMO inadvertently.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-46a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-46a-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-46a-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e1b9cb4963c41b37a19de624f8f2422bb9b227a8424e3a4670ba6532f8ad9bd2",
      "skos:note": "Regulator's satisfaction required for GMO licence application"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-46a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "46A Division does not apply to an application relating to inadvertent",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 46,
      "values:originalText": "dealings\nDespite section 46, this Division does not apply to an application\nfor a GMO licence if the Regulator is satisfied that:\n(a) the dealings proposed to be authorised by the licence are\nlimited to one or more of the following for purposes relating\nto disposing of a GMO:\n(i) conducting experiments with the GMO;\n(ii) propagating the GMO;\n(iii) growing, raising or culturing the GMO;\n(iv) transporting the GMO;\n(v) any other dealings to be undertaken for the purposes of,\nor for purposes relating to, disposing of the GMO; and\n(b) the applicant for the licence came into possession of the\nGMO inadvertently."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-46a-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-46a"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-46a-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Regulator has an obligation to satisfy the conditions for a GMO licence application",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Regulator must be satisfied that...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...the dealings proposed are limited to certain purposes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-46a-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "TemporalOverlap",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Regulator's satisfaction is conditional on the GMO being inadvertently obtained",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The applicant came into possession of the GMO...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...inadvertently"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-47",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "47 What the Regulator must do in relation to application",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-47"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.46",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Before issuing the licence, the Regulator must prepare a risk\nassessment and a risk management plan in relation to the dealings\nproposed to be authorised by the licence.\n\n\nLicensing system  Part 5\nInitial consideration of licences for dealings not involving intentional release of a GMO\ninto the environment  Division 3\nSection 47\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(2) In preparing the risk assessment, the Regulator must take into\naccount the risks posed by the dealings proposed to be authorised\nby the licence, including any risks to the health and safety of\npeople or risks to the environment.\n(3) In preparing the risk management plan, the Regulator must take\ninto account the means of managing any risks posed by the\ndealings proposed to be authorised by the licence in such a way as\nto protect:\n(a) the health and safety of people; and\n(b) the environment.\n(4) The Regulator may consult:\n(a) the States; and\n(b) the Gene Technology Technical Advisory Committee; and\n(c) relevant Commonwealth authorities or agencies; and\n(d) any local council that the Regulator considers appropriate;\nand\n(e) any other person the Regulator considers appropriate;\non any aspect of the application.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Before issuing the licence, the Regulator must prepare a risk\nassessment and a risk management plan in relation to the dealings\nproposed to be authorised by the licence.\n\n\nLicensing system  Part 5\nInitial consideration of licences for dealings not involving intentional release of a GMO\ninto the environment  Division 3\nSection 47\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(2) In preparing the risk assessment, the Regulator must take into\naccount the risks posed by the dealings proposed to be authorised\nby the licence, including any risks to the health and safety of\npeople or risks to the environment.\n(3) In preparing the risk management plan, the Regulator must take\ninto account the means of managing any risks posed by the\ndealings proposed to be authorised by the licence in such a way as\nto protect:\n(a) the health and safety of people; and\n(b) the environment.\n(4) The Regulator may consult:\n(a) the States; and\n(b) the Gene Technology Technical Advisory Committee; and\n(c) relevant Commonwealth authorities or agencies; and\n(d) any local council that the Regulator considers appropriate;\nand\n(e) any other person the Regulator considers appropriate;\non any aspect of the application.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-47-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-47-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-47-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-47-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "aa239c08cfaa88b35b5c0db4d4f87b0ff2f0e27aa67932d72440aa691e6bb70c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-47",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "47 What the Regulator must do in relation to application",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 46,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Before issuing the licence, the Regulator must prepare a risk\nassessment and a risk management plan in relation to the dealings\nproposed to be authorised by the licence.\n\n\nLicensing system  Part 5\nInitial consideration of licences for dealings not involving intentional release of a GMO\ninto the environment  Division 3\nSection 47\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(2) In preparing the risk assessment, the Regulator must take into\naccount the risks posed by the dealings proposed to be authorised\nby the licence, including any risks to the health and safety of\npeople or risks to the environment.\n(3) In preparing the risk management plan, the Regulator must take\ninto account the means of managing any risks posed by the\ndealings proposed to be authorised by the licence in such a way as\nto protect:\n(a) the health and safety of people; and\n(b) the environment.\n(4) The Regulator may consult:\n(a) the States; and\n(b) the Gene Technology Technical Advisory Committee; and\n(c) relevant Commonwealth authorities or agencies; and\n(d) any local council that the Regulator considers appropriate;\nand\n(e) any other person the Regulator considers appropriate;\non any aspect of the application."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-47-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "47(1) What the Regulator must do in relation to application",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
