    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-50",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "50 Regulator must prepare risk assessment and risk management",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-50"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.48",
      "values:originalText": "plan\n(1) Before issuing the licence, the Regulator must prepare a risk\nassessment and a risk management plan in relation to the dealings\nproposed to be authorised by the licence.\n\n\nLicensing system  Part 5\nInitial consideration of licences for dealings involving intentional release of a GMO into\nthe environment  Division 4\nSection 50A\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(3) Unless section 50A applies in relation to the application for the\nlicence, the Regulator must seek advice on matters relevant to the\npreparation of the risk assessment and the risk management plan\nfrom:\n(a) the States; and\n(b) the Gene Technology Technical Advisory Committee; and\n(c) each Commonwealth authority or agency prescribed by the\nregulations for the purposes of this paragraph; and\n(d) the Environment Minister; and\n(e) any local council that the Regulator considers appropriate.",
      "skos:definition": "plan\n(1) Before issuing the licence, the Regulator must prepare a risk\nassessment and a risk management plan in relation to the dealings\nproposed to be authorised by the licence.\n\n\nLicensing system  Part 5\nInitial consideration of licences for dealings involving intentional release of a GMO into\nthe environment  Division 4\nSection 50A\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(3) Unless section 50A applies in relation to the application for the\nlicence, the Regulator must seek advice on matters relevant to the\npreparation of the risk assessment and the risk management plan\nfrom:\n(a) the States; and\n(b) the Gene Technology Technical Advisory Committee; and\n(c) each Commonwealth authority or agency prescribed by the\nregulations for the purposes of this paragraph; and\n(d) the Environment Minister; and\n(e) any local council that the Regulator considers appropriate.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-50-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-50-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "64879f7d6b960a01909762d911a32d4582c20010c5641ee90278b644a9e3b525"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-50",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "50 Regulator must prepare risk assessment and risk management",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 48,
      "values:originalText": "plan\n(1) Before issuing the licence, the Regulator must prepare a risk\nassessment and a risk management plan in relation to the dealings\nproposed to be authorised by the licence.\n\n\nLicensing system  Part 5\nInitial consideration of licences for dealings involving intentional release of a GMO into\nthe environment  Division 4\nSection 50A\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(3) Unless section 50A applies in relation to the application for the\nlicence, the Regulator must seek advice on matters relevant to the\npreparation of the risk assessment and the risk management plan\nfrom:\n(a) the States; and\n(b) the Gene Technology Technical Advisory Committee; and\n(c) each Commonwealth authority or agency prescribed by the\nregulations for the purposes of this paragraph; and\n(d) the Environment Minister; and\n(e) any local council that the Regulator considers appropriate."
    },
