    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-50a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "50A Limited and controlled release applications",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-50a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.49",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to an application for a licence if the Regulator\nis satisfied that:\n(a) the principal purpose of the application is to enable the\nlicence holder, and persons covered by the licence, to\nconduct experiments; and\n(b) the application proposes, in relation to any GMO in respect\nof which dealings are proposed to be authorised:\n(i) controls to restrict the dissemination or persistence of\nthe GMO and its genetic material in the environment;\nand\n(ii) limits on the proposed release of the GMO; and\n(c) the Regulator is satisfied that the controls and limits are of\nsuch a kind that it is appropriate for the Regulator not to seek\nthe advice referred to in subsection 50(3).\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1):\ncontrols, in relation to a GMO and its genetic material, include the\nfollowing:\n(a) methods to restrict the dissemination or persistence of the\nGMO or its genetic material in the environment;\n(b) methods for disposal of the GMO or its genetic material;",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies to an application for a licence if the Regulator\nis satisfied that:\n(a) the principal purpose of the application is to enable the\nlicence holder, and persons covered by the licence, to\nconduct experiments; and\n(b) the application proposes, in relation to any GMO in respect\nof which dealings are proposed to be authorised:\n(i) controls to restrict the dissemination or persistence of\nthe GMO and its genetic material in the environment;\nand\n(ii) limits on the proposed release of the GMO; and\n(c) the Regulator is satisfied that the controls and limits are of\nsuch a kind that it is appropriate for the Regulator not to seek\nthe advice referred to in subsection 50(3).\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1):\ncontrols, in relation to a GMO and its genetic material, include the\nfollowing:\n(a) methods to restrict the dissemination or persistence of the\nGMO or its genetic material in the environment;\n(b) methods for disposal of the GMO or its genetic material;",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-50a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-50a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5c1d15bea16cf27362e364f0a98ecfd9ac4ee73c8bc10efa0c7654eeb6a4b6f2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-50a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "50A Limited and controlled release applications",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 49,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to an application for a licence if the Regulator\nis satisfied that:\n(a) the principal purpose of the application is to enable the\nlicence holder, and persons covered by the licence, to\nconduct experiments; and\n(b) the application proposes, in relation to any GMO in respect\nof which dealings are proposed to be authorised:\n(i) controls to restrict the dissemination or persistence of\nthe GMO and its genetic material in the environment;\nand\n(ii) limits on the proposed release of the GMO; and\n(c) the Regulator is satisfied that the controls and limits are of\nsuch a kind that it is appropriate for the Regulator not to seek\nthe advice referred to in subsection 50(3).\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1):\ncontrols, in relation to a GMO and its genetic material, include the\nfollowing:\n(a) methods to restrict the dissemination or persistence of the\nGMO or its genetic material in the environment;\n(b) methods for disposal of the GMO or its genetic material;"
    },
