      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.51",
      "values:originalText": "(2) In preparing the risk management plan, the Regulator must take\ninto account the following:\n(a) the means of managing any risks posed by those dealings in\nsuch a way as to protect:\n(i) the health and safety of people; and\n(ii) the environment;\n(c) any advice in relation to the risk management plan provided\nby a State or a local council in response to a request under\nsubsection 50(3);\n(d) any advice in relation to the risk management plan provided\nby the Gene Technology Technical Advisory Committee in\nresponse to a request under subsection 50(3);",
      "skos:definition": "(2) In preparing the risk management plan, the Regulator must take\ninto account the following:\n(a) the means of managing any risks posed by those dealings in\nsuch a way as to protect:\n(i) the health and safety of people; and\n(ii) the environment;\n(c) any advice in relation to the risk management plan provided\nby a State or a local council in response to a request under\nsubsection 50(3);\n(d) any advice in relation to the risk management plan provided\nby the Gene Technology Technical Advisory Committee in\nresponse to a request under subsection 50(3);",
