      "cml:conclusionText": "Regulator makes an informed decision."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-56-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56(2) Regulator must not issue the licence unless satisfied as to risk",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-56-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.55",
      "values:originalText": "(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), the Regulator must have regard\nto the following:\n(a) the risk assessment prepared under section 47 or 50 in\nrelation to the dealings;\n(b) the risk management plan prepared under section 47 or 50 in\nrelation to the dealings;\n(c) any submissions received under section 52 in relation to the\nlicence;\n(d) any policy guidelines in force under section 23 that relate to:\n(i) risks that may be posed by the dealings proposed to be\nauthorised by the licence; or\n(ii) ways of managing such risks so as to protect the health\nand safety of people or to protect the environment.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), the Regulator must have regard\nto the following:\n(a) the risk assessment prepared under section 47 or 50 in\nrelation to the dealings;\n(b) the risk management plan prepared under section 47 or 50 in\nrelation to the dealings;\n(c) any submissions received under section 52 in relation to the\nlicence;\n(d) any policy guidelines in force under section 23 that relate to:\n(i) risks that may be posed by the dealings proposed to be\nauthorised by the licence; or\n(ii) ways of managing such risks so as to protect the health\nand safety of people or to protect the environment.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-56"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-56-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-56-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-56-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "eb65e5f1aee5ab1a6c77fd0b11c47611ba9a37d6d781d481834f90458939b5d3",
      "skos:note": "Regulator must have regard to certain factors when issuing a licence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-56-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56(2) Regulator must not issue the licence unless satisfied as to risk",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 55,
      "values:originalText": "(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), the Regulator must have regard\nto the following:\n(a) the risk assessment prepared under section 47 or 50 in\nrelation to the dealings;\n(b) the risk management plan prepared under section 47 or 50 in\nrelation to the dealings;\n(c) any submissions received under section 52 in relation to the\nlicence;\n(d) any policy guidelines in force under section 23 that relate to:\n(i) risks that may be posed by the dealings proposed to be\nauthorised by the licence; or\n(ii) ways of managing such risks so as to protect the health\nand safety of people or to protect the environment."
    },
    {
