    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-72",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "72 Regulator to notify of proposed suspension, cancellation or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-72"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.66",
      "values:originalText": "variation\n(1) Before suspending, cancelling or varying a licence under this\nDivision, the Regulator must give written notice of the proposed\nsuspension, cancellation or variation to the licence holder.\n(2) The notice:\n(a) must state that the Regulator proposes to suspend, cancel or\nvary the licence; and\n\n\nLicensing system  Part 5\nSuspension, cancellation and variation of licences  Division 7\nSection 72\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(b) may require the licence holder to give to the Regulator any\ninformation of a kind specified in the notice that is relevant\nto the proposed suspension, cancellation or variation; and\n(c) may invite the licence holder to make a written submission to\nthe Regulator about the proposed suspension, cancellation or\nvariation.\n(3) The notice must specify a period within which the licence holder:\n(a) must give the information referred to in paragraph (2)(b); and\n(b) may make a submission under paragraph (2)(c).\nThe period must not end earlier than 30 days after the day on\nwhich the notice was given.\n(4) In considering whether to suspend, cancel or vary a licence, the\nRegulator must have regard to any submission made under\nparagraph (2)(c).\n(5) This section does not apply to a suspension, cancellation or\nvariation requested by the licence holder.\n(6) This section does not apply to a suspension, cancellation or\nvariation of a licence if the Regulator considers that the\nsuspension, cancellation or variation is necessary in order to avoid\nan imminent risk of death, serious illness, serious injury or serious\ndamage to the environment.\n(7) This section does not apply to a variation of a licence if the\nRegulator is satisfied that the variation is of minor significance or\ncomplexity.",
      "skos:definition": "variation\n(1) Before suspending, cancelling or varying a licence under this\nDivision, the Regulator must give written notice of the proposed\nsuspension, cancellation or variation to the licence holder.\n(2) The notice:\n(a) must state that the Regulator proposes to suspend, cancel or\nvary the licence; and\n\n\nLicensing system  Part 5\nSuspension, cancellation and variation of licences  Division 7\nSection 72\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(b) may require the licence holder to give to the Regulator any\ninformation of a kind specified in the notice that is relevant\nto the proposed suspension, cancellation or variation; and\n(c) may invite the licence holder to make a written submission to\nthe Regulator about the proposed suspension, cancellation or\nvariation.\n(3) The notice must specify a period within which the licence holder:\n(a) must give the information referred to in paragraph (2)(b); and\n(b) may make a submission under paragraph (2)(c).\nThe period must not end earlier than 30 days after the day on\nwhich the notice was given.\n(4) In considering whether to suspend, cancel or vary a licence, the\nRegulator must have regard to any submission made under\nparagraph (2)(c).\n(5) This section does not apply to a suspension, cancellation or\nvariation requested by the licence holder.\n(6) This section does not apply to a suspension, cancellation or\nvariation of a licence if the Regulator considers that the\nsuspension, cancellation or variation is necessary in order to avoid\nan imminent risk of death, serious illness, serious injury or serious\ndamage to the environment.\n(7) This section does not apply to a variation of a licence if the\nRegulator is satisfied that the variation is of minor significance or\ncomplexity.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-72-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-72-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-72-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-72-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-72-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-72-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-72-ss-7"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "819b60bb250f24cb8222cb1134acdffe15269b43765f46571a845fa39a8ee7fb"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-72",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "72 Regulator to notify of proposed suspension, cancellation or",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 66,
      "values:originalText": "variation\n(1) Before suspending, cancelling or varying a licence under this\nDivision, the Regulator must give written notice of the proposed\nsuspension, cancellation or variation to the licence holder.\n(2) The notice:\n(a) must state that the Regulator proposes to suspend, cancel or\nvary the licence; and\n\n\nLicensing system  Part 5\nSuspension, cancellation and variation of licences  Division 7\nSection 72\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(b) may require the licence holder to give to the Regulator any\ninformation of a kind specified in the notice that is relevant\nto the proposed suspension, cancellation or variation; and\n(c) may invite the licence holder to make a written submission to\nthe Regulator about the proposed suspension, cancellation or\nvariation.\n(3) The notice must specify a period within which the licence holder:\n(a) must give the information referred to in paragraph (2)(b); and\n(b) may make a submission under paragraph (2)(c).\nThe period must not end earlier than 30 days after the day on\nwhich the notice was given.\n(4) In considering whether to suspend, cancel or vary a licence, the\nRegulator must have regard to any submission made under\nparagraph (2)(c).\n(5) This section does not apply to a suspension, cancellation or\nvariation requested by the licence holder.\n(6) This section does not apply to a suspension, cancellation or\nvariation of a licence if the Regulator considers that the\nsuspension, cancellation or variation is necessary in order to avoid\nan imminent risk of death, serious illness, serious injury or serious\ndamage to the environment.\n(7) This section does not apply to a variation of a licence if the\nRegulator is satisfied that the variation is of minor significance or\ncomplexity."
    },
