    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-72a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "72A Simplified outline",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-72a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.68",
      "values:originalText": "The following is a simplified outline of this Part:\nThis Part provides a system under which the Minister can make\ndeterminations relating to dealings with GMOs in emergencies.\n\n\nEmergency dealing determinations  Part 5A\nMaking of emergency dealing determination  Division 2\nSection 72B\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024",
      "skos:definition": "The following is a simplified outline of this Part:\nThis Part provides a system under which the Minister can make\ndeterminations relating to dealings with GMOs in emergencies.\n\n\nEmergency dealing determinations  Part 5A\nMaking of emergency dealing determination  Division 2\nSection 72B\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-72a-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6ec93e6af5269fa9f7ad3d491cc5726730ce67c2a50c3b0b58acc663f149213d",
      "skos:note": "Simplified outline of Part 5A"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-72a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "72A Simplified outline",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 68,
      "values:originalText": "The following is a simplified outline of this Part:\nThis Part provides a system under which the Minister can make\ndeterminations relating to dealings with GMOs in emergencies.\n\n\nEmergency dealing determinations  Part 5A\nMaking of emergency dealing determination  Division 2\nSection 72B\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-72a-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-72a"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-72b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "72B Minister may make emergency dealing determination",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-72b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.69",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument (an emergency\ndealing determination), specify dealings with a GMO for the\npurposes of this Part.\n(2) The Minister may make an emergency dealing determination only\nif:\n(a) the Minister has received advice from:\n(i) the Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer; or\n(ii) the Commonwealth Chief Veterinary Officer; or\n(iii) the Commonwealth Chief Plant Protection Officer; or\n(iv) a person prescribed by the regulations;\nthat there is an actual or imminent threat to the health and\nsafety of people or to the environment, and that the dealings\nproposed to be specified in the emergency dealing\ndetermination would, or would be likely to, adequately\naddress the threat; and\n(b) the Minister is satisfied that there is an actual or imminent\nthreat to the health and safety of people or to the\nenvironment, and that the dealings proposed to be specified\nin the emergency dealing determination would, or would be\nlikely to, adequately address the threat; and\n(c) the Minister has received advice from the Regulator that any\nrisks posed by the dealings proposed to be specified in the\nemergency dealing determination are able to be managed in\nsuch a way as:\n(i) to protect the health and safety of people; and\n(ii) to protect the environment; and\n(d) the Minister is satisfied that any risks posed by the dealings\nproposed to be specified in the emergency dealing\ndetermination are able to be managed in such a way as:\n(i) to protect the health and safety of people; and",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument (an emergency\ndealing determination), specify dealings with a GMO for the\npurposes of this Part.\n(2) The Minister may make an emergency dealing determination only\nif:\n(a) the Minister has received advice from:\n(i) the Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer; or\n(ii) the Commonwealth Chief Veterinary Officer; or\n(iii) the Commonwealth Chief Plant Protection Officer; or\n(iv) a person prescribed by the regulations;\nthat there is an actual or imminent threat to the health and\nsafety of people or to the environment, and that the dealings\nproposed to be specified in the emergency dealing\ndetermination would, or would be likely to, adequately\naddress the threat; and\n(b) the Minister is satisfied that there is an actual or imminent\nthreat to the health and safety of people or to the\nenvironment, and that the dealings proposed to be specified\nin the emergency dealing determination would, or would be\nlikely to, adequately address the threat; and\n(c) the Minister has received advice from the Regulator that any\nrisks posed by the dealings proposed to be specified in the\nemergency dealing determination are able to be managed in\nsuch a way as:\n(i) to protect the health and safety of people; and\n(ii) to protect the environment; and\n(d) the Minister is satisfied that any risks posed by the dealings\nproposed to be specified in the emergency dealing\ndetermination are able to be managed in such a way as:\n(i) to protect the health and safety of people; and",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-72b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-72b-ss-2"
        }
