      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.70",
      "values:originalText": "(5) The Minister may extend the period of effect of an emergency\ndealing determination only if:\n(a) the Minister has received advice from the original adviser in\nrelation to the emergency dealing determination that the\nthreat to which the determination relates still exists, and that\nthe proposed extension would, or would be likely to,\nadequately address the threat; and\n(b) the Minister is satisfied that the threat still exists, and that the\nproposed extension would, or would be likely to, adequately\naddress that threat; and\n(c) the Minister has received advice from the Regulator that any\nrisks posed by the proposed extension are able to be managed\nin such a way as:\n(i) to protect the health and safety of people; and\n(ii) to protect the environment; and\n(d) the Minister is satisfied that any risks posed by the proposed\nextension are able to be managed in such a way as:\n(i) to protect the health and safety of people; and\n(ii) to protect the environment; and\n(e) a majority of jurisdictions agree to the extension.",
