      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Regulator may suspend or cancel certification",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Reasonable grounds exist",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Certification suspension or cancellation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-89",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "89 Regulator to notify of proposed suspension, cancellation or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-89"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.86",
      "values:originalText": "variation\n(1) Before suspending, cancelling or varying a certification under this\nDivision, the Regulator must give written notice of the proposed\nsuspension, cancellation or variation to the holder of the\ncertification.\n(2) The notice:\n(a) must state that the Regulator proposes to suspend, cancel or\nvary the certification; and\n(b) may require the holder of the certification to give to the\nRegulator any information of a kind specified in the notice\nthat is relevant to the proposed suspension, cancellation or\nvariation; and\n(c) may invite the holder of the certification to make a written\nsubmission to the Regulator about the proposed suspension,\ncancellation or variation.\n\n\nCertification and accreditation  Part 7\nCertification  Division 2\nSection 89A\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(3) The notice must specify a period within which the holder of the\ncertification:\n(a) must give the information referred to in paragraph (2)(b); and\n(b) may make a submission under paragraph (2)(c).\nThe period must not end earlier than 30 days after the day on\nwhich the notice was given.\n(4) In considering whether to suspend, cancel or vary a certification,\nthe Regulator must have regard to any submission made under\nparagraph (2)(c).\n(5) This section does not apply to a suspension, cancellation or\nvariation requested by the holder of the certification.\n(6) This section does not apply to a suspension, cancellation or\nvariation of a certification if the Regulator considers that the\nsuspension, cancellation or variation is necessary in order to avoid\nan imminent risk of death, serious illness, serious injury or serious\ndamage to the environment.\n(7) This section does not apply to a variation of a certification if the\nRegulator is satisfied that the variation is of minor significance or\ncomplexity.",
      "skos:definition": "variation\n(1) Before suspending, cancelling or varying a certification under this\nDivision, the Regulator must give written notice of the proposed\nsuspension, cancellation or variation to the holder of the\ncertification.\n(2) The notice:\n(a) must state that the Regulator proposes to suspend, cancel or\nvary the certification; and\n(b) may require the holder of the certification to give to the\nRegulator any information of a kind specified in the notice\nthat is relevant to the proposed suspension, cancellation or\nvariation; and\n(c) may invite the holder of the certification to make a written\nsubmission to the Regulator about the proposed suspension,\ncancellation or variation.\n\n\nCertification and accreditation  Part 7\nCertification  Division 2\nSection 89A\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(3) The notice must specify a period within which the holder of the\ncertification:\n(a) must give the information referred to in paragraph (2)(b); and\n(b) may make a submission under paragraph (2)(c).\nThe period must not end earlier than 30 days after the day on\nwhich the notice was given.\n(4) In considering whether to suspend, cancel or vary a certification,\nthe Regulator must have regard to any submission made under\nparagraph (2)(c).\n(5) This section does not apply to a suspension, cancellation or\nvariation requested by the holder of the certification.\n(6) This section does not apply to a suspension, cancellation or\nvariation of a certification if the Regulator considers that the\nsuspension, cancellation or variation is necessary in order to avoid\nan imminent risk of death, serious illness, serious injury or serious\ndamage to the environment.\n(7) This section does not apply to a variation of a certification if the\nRegulator is satisfied that the variation is of minor significance or\ncomplexity.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-89-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-89-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-89-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-89-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-89-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-89-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-89-ss-7"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "819b60bb250f24cb8222cb1134acdffe15269b43765f46571a845fa39a8ee7fb"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-89",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "89 Regulator to notify of proposed suspension, cancellation or",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 86,
      "values:originalText": "variation\n(1) Before suspending, cancelling or varying a certification under this\nDivision, the Regulator must give written notice of the proposed\nsuspension, cancellation or variation to the holder of the\ncertification.\n(2) The notice:\n(a) must state that the Regulator proposes to suspend, cancel or\nvary the certification; and\n(b) may require the holder of the certification to give to the\nRegulator any information of a kind specified in the notice\nthat is relevant to the proposed suspension, cancellation or\nvariation; and\n(c) may invite the holder of the certification to make a written\nsubmission to the Regulator about the proposed suspension,\ncancellation or variation.\n\n\nCertification and accreditation  Part 7\nCertification  Division 2\nSection 89A\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(3) The notice must specify a period within which the holder of the\ncertification:\n(a) must give the information referred to in paragraph (2)(b); and\n(b) may make a submission under paragraph (2)(c).\nThe period must not end earlier than 30 days after the day on\nwhich the notice was given.\n(4) In considering whether to suspend, cancel or vary a certification,\nthe Regulator must have regard to any submission made under\nparagraph (2)(c).\n(5) This section does not apply to a suspension, cancellation or\nvariation requested by the holder of the certification.\n(6) This section does not apply to a suspension, cancellation or\nvariation of a certification if the Regulator considers that the\nsuspension, cancellation or variation is necessary in order to avoid\nan imminent risk of death, serious illness, serious injury or serious\ndamage to the environment.\n(7) This section does not apply to a variation of a certification if the\nRegulator is satisfied that the variation is of minor significance or\ncomplexity."
    },
