    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-92",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "92 Regulator may accredit organisations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-92"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.89",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Regulator may, by written instrument, accredit an organisation\nas an accredited organisation.\n(2) In deciding whether to accredit an organisation, the Regulator must\nhave regard to:\n(a) whether the organisation has established an Institutional\nBiosafety Committee in accordance with written guidelines\nissued by the Regulator under section 98; and\n(b) if the organisation has established an Institutional Biosafety\nCommittee—whether the organisation will be able to\nmaintain the Institutional Biosafety Committee in accordance\nwith such guidelines; and\n(c) if the organisation has established an Institutional Biosafety\nCommittee—whether the organisation has appropriate\nindemnity arrangements for its Institutional Biosafety\nCommittee members; and",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Regulator may, by written instrument, accredit an organisation\nas an accredited organisation.\n(2) In deciding whether to accredit an organisation, the Regulator must\nhave regard to:\n(a) whether the organisation has established an Institutional\nBiosafety Committee in accordance with written guidelines\nissued by the Regulator under section 98; and\n(b) if the organisation has established an Institutional Biosafety\nCommittee—whether the organisation will be able to\nmaintain the Institutional Biosafety Committee in accordance\nwith such guidelines; and\n(c) if the organisation has established an Institutional Biosafety\nCommittee—whether the organisation has appropriate\nindemnity arrangements for its Institutional Biosafety\nCommittee members; and",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-92-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-92-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d8fe5ad202b28e67776c0f4c5a24f3420bb8f5fb46ca3cab74723b56cf116b17"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-92",
