      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-96-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits suspension or cancellation of accreditation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Regulator may, by notice in writing...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The accreditation of an organisation shall not be suspended or cancelled."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-96-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Overlap",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Overlaps with accreditation duration",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Regulator may, by notice in writing...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Suspension or cancellation of accreditation occurs during the accreditation period."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-97",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "97 Regulator to notify of proposed suspension, cancellation or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-97"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.91",
      "values:originalText": "variation\n(1) Before suspending, cancelling or varying an accreditation under\nthis Division, the Regulator must give written notice of the\nproposed suspension, cancellation or variation to the holder of the\naccreditation.\n(2) The notice:\n(a) must state that the Regulator proposes to suspend, cancel or\nvary the accreditation; and\n(b) may require the holder of the accreditation to give to the\nRegulator any information of a kind specified in the notice\nthat is relevant to the proposed suspension, cancellation or\nvariation; and\n(c) may invite the holder of the accreditation to make a written\nsubmission to the Regulator about the proposed suspension,\ncancellation or variation.\n(3) The notice must specify a period within which the holder of the\naccreditation:\n(a) must give the information referred to in paragraph (2)(b); and\n(b) may make a submission under paragraph (2)(c).\nThe period must not end earlier than 30 days after the day on\nwhich the notice was given.\n(4) In considering whether to suspend, cancel or vary an accreditation,\nthe Regulator must have regard to any submission made under\nparagraph (2)(c).",
      "skos:definition": "variation\n(1) Before suspending, cancelling or varying an accreditation under\nthis Division, the Regulator must give written notice of the\nproposed suspension, cancellation or variation to the holder of the\naccreditation.\n(2) The notice:\n(a) must state that the Regulator proposes to suspend, cancel or\nvary the accreditation; and\n(b) may require the holder of the accreditation to give to the\nRegulator any information of a kind specified in the notice\nthat is relevant to the proposed suspension, cancellation or\nvariation; and\n(c) may invite the holder of the accreditation to make a written\nsubmission to the Regulator about the proposed suspension,\ncancellation or variation.\n(3) The notice must specify a period within which the holder of the\naccreditation:\n(a) must give the information referred to in paragraph (2)(b); and\n(b) may make a submission under paragraph (2)(c).\nThe period must not end earlier than 30 days after the day on\nwhich the notice was given.\n(4) In considering whether to suspend, cancel or vary an accreditation,\nthe Regulator must have regard to any submission made under\nparagraph (2)(c).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-97-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-97-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-97-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-97-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "819b60bb250f24cb8222cb1134acdffe15269b43765f46571a845fa39a8ee7fb"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-97",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "97 Regulator to notify of proposed suspension, cancellation or",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 91,
      "values:originalText": "variation\n(1) Before suspending, cancelling or varying an accreditation under\nthis Division, the Regulator must give written notice of the\nproposed suspension, cancellation or variation to the holder of the\naccreditation.\n(2) The notice:\n(a) must state that the Regulator proposes to suspend, cancel or\nvary the accreditation; and\n(b) may require the holder of the accreditation to give to the\nRegulator any information of a kind specified in the notice\nthat is relevant to the proposed suspension, cancellation or\nvariation; and\n(c) may invite the holder of the accreditation to make a written\nsubmission to the Regulator about the proposed suspension,\ncancellation or variation.\n(3) The notice must specify a period within which the holder of the\naccreditation:\n(a) must give the information referred to in paragraph (2)(b); and\n(b) may make a submission under paragraph (2)(c).\nThe period must not end earlier than 30 days after the day on\nwhich the notice was given.\n(4) In considering whether to suspend, cancel or vary an accreditation,\nthe Regulator must have regard to any submission made under\nparagraph (2)(c)."
    },
