    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-103",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "103 Remuneration",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-103"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.96",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person who is a member of the Gene Technology Technical\nAdvisory Committee or an expert adviser is to be paid the\nremuneration that is determined by the Remuneration Tribunal. If\nno determination of that remuneration by the Tribunal is in\noperation, the member is to be paid the remuneration that is\nprescribed by the regulations.\n(2) A person who is a member of the Gene Technology Technical\nAdvisory Committee or an expert adviser is to be paid the\nallowances that are prescribed by the regulations.\n(3) This section has effect subject to the Remuneration Tribunal Act\n1973.\n\n\nThe Gene Technology Technical Advisory Committee and the Gene Technology Ethics\nand Community Consultative Committee  Part 8\nThe Gene Technology Technical Advisory Committee  Division 2\nSection 104\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person who is a member of the Gene Technology Technical\nAdvisory Committee or an expert adviser is to be paid the\nremuneration that is determined by the Remuneration Tribunal. If\nno determination of that remuneration by the Tribunal is in\noperation, the member is to be paid the remuneration that is\nprescribed by the regulations.\n(2) A person who is a member of the Gene Technology Technical\nAdvisory Committee or an expert adviser is to be paid the\nallowances that are prescribed by the regulations.\n(3) This section has effect subject to the Remuneration Tribunal Act\n1973.\n\n\nThe Gene Technology Technical Advisory Committee and the Gene Technology Ethics\nand Community Consultative Committee  Part 8\nThe Gene Technology Technical Advisory Committee  Division 2\nSection 104\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024",
      "cml:hasPart": [
