    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-104",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "104 Members and procedures",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-104"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.97",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The regulations may prescribe matters relating to the members of\nthe Gene Technology Technical Advisory Committee and expert\nadvisers, including, but not limited to, the following:\n(a) term of appointment;\n(b) resignation;\n(c) disclosure of interests;\n(d) termination of appointment;\n(e) leave of absence.\n(2) The regulations may prescribe matters relating to the operation of\nthe Gene Technology Technical Advisory Committee, including,\nbut not limited to:\n(a) procedures for convening meetings of the Committee; and\n(b) the constitution of a quorum for a meeting of the Committee;\nand\n(c) the way in which matters are to be resolved by the\nCommittee; and\n(d) Committee records; and\n(e) reporting requirements, including, but not limited to, reports\nto the Regulator and to the public.\n(3) If no regulations are in force under subsection (2), the Committee\nmust operate in the way determined by the Regulator in writing.\n(4) If no regulations are in force under subsection (2) and no\ndetermination is in force under subsection (3), the Committee may\noperate in the way it determines.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The regulations may prescribe matters relating to the members of\nthe Gene Technology Technical Advisory Committee and expert\nadvisers, including, but not limited to, the following:\n(a) term of appointment;\n(b) resignation;\n(c) disclosure of interests;\n(d) termination of appointment;\n(e) leave of absence.\n(2) The regulations may prescribe matters relating to the operation of\nthe Gene Technology Technical Advisory Committee, including,\nbut not limited to:\n(a) procedures for convening meetings of the Committee; and\n(b) the constitution of a quorum for a meeting of the Committee;\nand\n(c) the way in which matters are to be resolved by the\nCommittee; and\n(d) Committee records; and\n(e) reporting requirements, including, but not limited to, reports\nto the Regulator and to the public.\n(3) If no regulations are in force under subsection (2), the Committee\nmust operate in the way determined by the Regulator in writing.\n(4) If no regulations are in force under subsection (2) and no\ndetermination is in force under subsection (3), the Committee may\noperate in the way it determines.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-104-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-104-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-104-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-104-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6f9ba7d65ddb21e004df3d11388c76907fabc307b2ff7526a7eb4310d5870be8"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-104",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "104 Members and procedures",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 97,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The regulations may prescribe matters relating to the members of\nthe Gene Technology Technical Advisory Committee and expert\nadvisers, including, but not limited to, the following:\n(a) term of appointment;\n(b) resignation;\n(c) disclosure of interests;\n(d) termination of appointment;\n(e) leave of absence.\n(2) The regulations may prescribe matters relating to the operation of\nthe Gene Technology Technical Advisory Committee, including,\nbut not limited to:\n(a) procedures for convening meetings of the Committee; and\n(b) the constitution of a quorum for a meeting of the Committee;\nand\n(c) the way in which matters are to be resolved by the\nCommittee; and\n(d) Committee records; and\n(e) reporting requirements, including, but not limited to, reports\nto the Regulator and to the public.\n(3) If no regulations are in force under subsection (2), the Committee\nmust operate in the way determined by the Regulator in writing.\n(4) If no regulations are in force under subsection (2) and no\ndetermination is in force under subsection (3), the Committee may\noperate in the way it determines."
    },
