    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-110",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "110 Membership and Procedures",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-110"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.100",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The regulations may prescribe matters relating to the members of\nthe Ethics and Community Committee, including, but not limited\nto, the following:\n(a) term of appointment;\n(b) resignation;\n\n\nThe Gene Technology Technical Advisory Committee and the Gene Technology Ethics\nand Community Consultative Committee  Part 8\nThe Gene Technology Ethics and Community Consultative Committee  Division 3\nSection 111\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(c) disclosure of interests;\n(d) termination of appointment;\n(e) leave of absence.\n(2) The regulations may prescribe matters relating to the operation of\nthe Ethics and Community Committee, including, but not limited\nto, the following:\n(a) procedures for convening meetings of the Ethics and\nCommunity Committee;\n(b) the constitution of a quorum for a meeting of the Ethics and\nCommunity Committee;\n(c) the way in which matters are to be resolved by the Ethics and\nCommunity Committee;\n(d) Ethics and Community Committee records;\n(e) reporting requirements, including, but not limited to, reports\nto the Regulator and to the public.\n(3) If no regulations are in force under subsection (2), the Ethics and\nCommunity Committee must operate in the way determined in\nwriting by the Regulator.\n(4) If no regulations are in force under subsection (2) and no\ndetermination is in force under subsection (3), the Ethics and\nCommunity Committee may operate in the way determined in\nwriting by the Ethics and Community Committee.\n(5) A determination made under subsection (3) or (4) is not a\nlegislative instrument.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The regulations may prescribe matters relating to the members of\nthe Ethics and Community Committee, including, but not limited\nto, the following:\n(a) term of appointment;\n(b) resignation;\n\n\nThe Gene Technology Technical Advisory Committee and the Gene Technology Ethics\nand Community Consultative Committee  Part 8\nThe Gene Technology Ethics and Community Consultative Committee  Division 3\nSection 111\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(c) disclosure of interests;\n(d) termination of appointment;\n(e) leave of absence.\n(2) The regulations may prescribe matters relating to the operation of\nthe Ethics and Community Committee, including, but not limited\nto, the following:\n(a) procedures for convening meetings of the Ethics and\nCommunity Committee;\n(b) the constitution of a quorum for a meeting of the Ethics and\nCommunity Committee;\n(c) the way in which matters are to be resolved by the Ethics and\nCommunity Committee;\n(d) Ethics and Community Committee records;\n(e) reporting requirements, including, but not limited to, reports\nto the Regulator and to the public.\n(3) If no regulations are in force under subsection (2), the Ethics and\nCommunity Committee must operate in the way determined in\nwriting by the Regulator.\n(4) If no regulations are in force under subsection (2) and no\ndetermination is in force under subsection (3), the Ethics and\nCommunity Committee may operate in the way determined in\nwriting by the Ethics and Community Committee.\n(5) A determination made under subsection (3) or (4) is not a\nlegislative instrument.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-110-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-110-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-110-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-110-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-110-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dfcba5dc0cff3b0ad0a14a8bf0bb2c8da431321dcc939f9c93b7c0b1c631b213"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-110",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "110 Membership and Procedures",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 100,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The regulations may prescribe matters relating to the members of\nthe Ethics and Community Committee, including, but not limited\nto, the following:\n(a) term of appointment;\n(b) resignation;\n\n\nThe Gene Technology Technical Advisory Committee and the Gene Technology Ethics\nand Community Consultative Committee  Part 8\nThe Gene Technology Ethics and Community Consultative Committee  Division 3\nSection 111\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(c) disclosure of interests;\n(d) termination of appointment;\n(e) leave of absence.\n(2) The regulations may prescribe matters relating to the operation of\nthe Ethics and Community Committee, including, but not limited\nto, the following:\n(a) procedures for convening meetings of the Ethics and\nCommunity Committee;\n(b) the constitution of a quorum for a meeting of the Ethics and\nCommunity Committee;\n(c) the way in which matters are to be resolved by the Ethics and\nCommunity Committee;\n(d) Ethics and Community Committee records;\n(e) reporting requirements, including, but not limited to, reports\nto the Regulator and to the public.\n(3) If no regulations are in force under subsection (2), the Ethics and\nCommunity Committee must operate in the way determined in\nwriting by the Regulator.\n(4) If no regulations are in force under subsection (2) and no\ndetermination is in force under subsection (3), the Ethics and\nCommunity Committee may operate in the way determined in\nwriting by the Ethics and Community Committee.\n(5) A determination made under subsection (3) or (4) is not a\nlegislative instrument."
    },
