        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-118",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "118 Appointment of the Regulator",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-118"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.104",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Regulator is to be appointed by the Governor-General by\nwritten instrument.\n(2) The Regulator holds office for the period specified in the\ninstrument of appointment. The period specified must not be less\nthan 3 years or more than 5 years.\n(3) The Regulator holds office on a full-time basis.\n(4) The Governor-General must not appoint a person as the Regulator\nunless a majority of jurisdictions agree to the appointment.\n(5) The Governor-General must not appoint a person as the Regulator\nif, at any time during the period of 2 years immediately before the\nproposed period of appointment, the person was employed by a\nbody corporate whose primary commercial activity relates directly\nto the development and implementation of gene technologies.\n(6) The Governor-General must not appoint a person as the Regulator\nif the person has a pecuniary interest in a body corporate whose\nprimary commercial activity relates directly to the development\nand implementation of gene technologies.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Regulator is to be appointed by the Governor-General by\nwritten instrument.\n(2) The Regulator holds office for the period specified in the\ninstrument of appointment. The period specified must not be less\nthan 3 years or more than 5 years.\n(3) The Regulator holds office on a full-time basis.\n(4) The Governor-General must not appoint a person as the Regulator\nunless a majority of jurisdictions agree to the appointment.\n(5) The Governor-General must not appoint a person as the Regulator\nif, at any time during the period of 2 years immediately before the\nproposed period of appointment, the person was employed by a\nbody corporate whose primary commercial activity relates directly\nto the development and implementation of gene technologies.\n(6) The Governor-General must not appoint a person as the Regulator\nif the person has a pecuniary interest in a body corporate whose\nprimary commercial activity relates directly to the development\nand implementation of gene technologies.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-118-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-118-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-118-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-118-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-118-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-118-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "be03c7cf2ec93b2fb5029ffd2f829e0ff54e1c04c0218e0d7e825ccc968fb13e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-118",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "118 Appointment of the Regulator",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 104,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Regulator is to be appointed by the Governor-General by\nwritten instrument.\n(2) The Regulator holds office for the period specified in the\ninstrument of appointment. The period specified must not be less\nthan 3 years or more than 5 years.\n(3) The Regulator holds office on a full-time basis.\n(4) The Governor-General must not appoint a person as the Regulator\nunless a majority of jurisdictions agree to the appointment.\n(5) The Governor-General must not appoint a person as the Regulator\nif, at any time during the period of 2 years immediately before the\nproposed period of appointment, the person was employed by a\nbody corporate whose primary commercial activity relates directly\nto the development and implementation of gene technologies.\n(6) The Governor-General must not appoint a person as the Regulator\nif the person has a pecuniary interest in a body corporate whose\nprimary commercial activity relates directly to the development\nand implementation of gene technologies."
    },
