      },
      "cml:operator": ">=",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Regulator's retirement must occur after removal or retirement due to incapacity.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(5) For the purposes of the Superannuation Act 1976, the Regulator is taken to have been retired from office on the grounds of invalidity..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-119-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "119(6) Termination of appointment",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-119-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.104",
      "values:originalText": "(6) For the purposes of the Superannuation Act 1990, the Regulator is\ntaken to have been retired from office on the grounds of invalidity\nif:\n(a) the Regulator is removed or retired from office on the\ngrounds of physical or mental incapacity; and\n(b) CSC gives a certificate under section 13 of that Act.",
      "skos:definition": "(6) For the purposes of the Superannuation Act 1990, the Regulator is\ntaken to have been retired from office on the grounds of invalidity\nif:\n(a) the Regulator is removed or retired from office on the\ngrounds of physical or mental incapacity; and\n(b) CSC gives a certificate under section 13 of that Act.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-119"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-119-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-119-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ad566a55cfdd760344913ccf68784f1d628e022148615a4351cd8534bbd93f44",
      "skos:note": "Regulator must be retired on grounds of invalidity if removed or retired due to incapacity and CSC gives a certificate."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-119-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "119(6) Termination of appointment",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 104,
      "values:originalText": "(6) For the purposes of the Superannuation Act 1990, the Regulator is\ntaken to have been retired from office on the grounds of invalidity\nif:\n(a) the Regulator is removed or retired from office on the\ngrounds of physical or mental incapacity; and\n(b) CSC gives a certificate under section 13 of that Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-119-ss-6-norm",
