    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-145",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "145 Simplified outline",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-145"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.118",
      "values:originalText": "The following is a simplified outline of this Part:\nThis Part enables the Regulator to give directions to a licence\nholder or to a person covered by a licence, if:\n(a)\nthe Regulator believes that the person is not\ncomplying with this Act or the regulations; and\n(b)\nthe Regulator believes that it is necessary to do so\nin order to protect the health and safety of people\nor to protect the environment, or for certain other\nreasons.\nThis Part enables the Regulator to give directions to a person\npermitted by an emergency dealing determination to deal with a\nGMO, if:\n(a)\nthe Regulator believes that the person is not\ncomplying with this Act or the regulations; and\n(b)\nthe Regulator believes that it is necessary to do so\nin order to protect the health and safety of people\nor to protect the environment or for certain other\nreasons.\nThe Part also empowers the Federal Court to issue injunctions, and\ncontains a forfeiture provision.",
      "skos:definition": "The following is a simplified outline of this Part:\nThis Part enables the Regulator to give directions to a licence\nholder or to a person covered by a licence, if:\n(a)\nthe Regulator believes that the person is not\ncomplying with this Act or the regulations; and\n(b)\nthe Regulator believes that it is necessary to do so\nin order to protect the health and safety of people\nor to protect the environment, or for certain other\nreasons.\nThis Part enables the Regulator to give directions to a person\npermitted by an emergency dealing determination to deal with a\nGMO, if:\n(a)\nthe Regulator believes that the person is not\ncomplying with this Act or the regulations; and\n(b)\nthe Regulator believes that it is necessary to do so\nin order to protect the health and safety of people\nor to protect the environment or for certain other\nreasons.\nThe Part also empowers the Federal Court to issue injunctions, and\ncontains a forfeiture provision.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-145-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-145-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c110dc5738913e6aa787e9ed61cb8baab8be193695545290e3cac81056655509",
      "skos:note": "Regulator can give directions to comply with Act or regulations."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-145",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "145 Simplified outline",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 118,
      "values:originalText": "The following is a simplified outline of this Part:\nThis Part enables the Regulator to give directions to a licence\nholder or to a person covered by a licence, if:\n(a)\nthe Regulator believes that the person is not\ncomplying with this Act or the regulations; and\n(b)\nthe Regulator believes that it is necessary to do so\nin order to protect the health and safety of people\nor to protect the environment, or for certain other\nreasons.\nThis Part enables the Regulator to give directions to a person\npermitted by an emergency dealing determination to deal with a\nGMO, if:\n(a)\nthe Regulator believes that the person is not\ncomplying with this Act or the regulations; and\n(b)\nthe Regulator believes that it is necessary to do so\nin order to protect the health and safety of people\nor to protect the environment or for certain other\nreasons.\nThe Part also empowers the Federal Court to issue injunctions, and\ncontains a forfeiture provision."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-145-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-145"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-145-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "can",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Regulator has the power to give directions.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-146",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "146 Regulator may give directions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-146"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.118",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Regulator believes, on reasonable grounds, that:\n\n\nEnforcement  Part 10\n\nSection 146\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(a) a licence holder is not complying with this Act or the\nregulations in respect of a thing; and\n(b) either of the following applies:\n(i) it is necessary to exercise powers under this section in\norder to protect the health and safety of people or to\nprotect the environment;\n(ii) it is desirable in the public interest, having regard to the\nmatters specified in subsection (2A), for the Regulator\nto exercise powers under this section;\nthe Regulator may give directions to the licence holder, by written\nnotice, requiring the licence holder, within the time specified in the\nnotice, to take such steps in relation to the thing as are reasonable\nin the circumstances for the licence holder to comply with this Act\nor the regulations.\n(2) If the Regulator believes on reasonable grounds that:\n(a) one of the following kinds of persons is not complying with\nthis Act or the regulations in respect of a thing:\n(i) a person covered by a GMO licence;\n(ii) a person dealing with, or who has dealt with, a GMO\nspecified in an emergency dealing determination; and\n(b) either of the following applies:\n(i) it is necessary to exercise powers under this section in\norder to protect the health and safety of people or to\nprotect the environment;\n(ii) it is desirable in the public interest, having regard to the\nmatters specified in subsection (2A), for the Regulator\nto exercise powers under this section;\nthe Regulator may give directions to the person, by written notice,\nrequiring the person, within the time specified in the notice, to take\nsuch steps in relation to the thing as are reasonable in the\ncircumstances for the person to comply with this Act or the\nregulations.\n(2A) For the purposes of deciding under subparagraph (1)(b)(ii) or\n(2)(b)(ii) whether it is desirable to exercise powers under this",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the Regulator believes, on reasonable grounds, that:\n\n\nEnforcement  Part 10\n\nSection 146\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(a) a licence holder is not complying with this Act or the\nregulations in respect of a thing; and\n(b) either of the following applies:\n(i) it is necessary to exercise powers under this section in\norder to protect the health and safety of people or to\nprotect the environment;\n(ii) it is desirable in the public interest, having regard to the\nmatters specified in subsection (2A), for the Regulator\nto exercise powers under this section;\nthe Regulator may give directions to the licence holder, by written\nnotice, requiring the licence holder, within the time specified in the\nnotice, to take such steps in relation to the thing as are reasonable\nin the circumstances for the licence holder to comply with this Act\nor the regulations.\n(2) If the Regulator believes on reasonable grounds that:\n(a) one of the following kinds of persons is not complying with\nthis Act or the regulations in respect of a thing:\n(i) a person covered by a GMO licence;\n(ii) a person dealing with, or who has dealt with, a GMO\nspecified in an emergency dealing determination; and\n(b) either of the following applies:\n(i) it is necessary to exercise powers under this section in\norder to protect the health and safety of people or to\nprotect the environment;\n(ii) it is desirable in the public interest, having regard to the\nmatters specified in subsection (2A), for the Regulator\nto exercise powers under this section;\nthe Regulator may give directions to the person, by written notice,\nrequiring the person, within the time specified in the notice, to take\nsuch steps in relation to the thing as are reasonable in the\ncircumstances for the person to comply with this Act or the\nregulations.\n(2A) For the purposes of deciding under subparagraph (1)(b)(ii) or\n(2)(b)(ii) whether it is desirable to exercise powers under this",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-146-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-146-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-146-ss-2a"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "efe9b1052767fc2332ccf235e3838e97e09c4fb156f92a7ec5116a7dd263087d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-146",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "146 Regulator may give directions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 118,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Regulator believes, on reasonable grounds, that:\n\n\nEnforcement  Part 10\n\nSection 146\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(a) a licence holder is not complying with this Act or the\nregulations in respect of a thing; and\n(b) either of the following applies:\n(i) it is necessary to exercise powers under this section in\norder to protect the health and safety of people or to\nprotect the environment;\n(ii) it is desirable in the public interest, having regard to the\nmatters specified in subsection (2A), for the Regulator\nto exercise powers under this section;\nthe Regulator may give directions to the licence holder, by written\nnotice, requiring the licence holder, within the time specified in the\nnotice, to take such steps in relation to the thing as are reasonable\nin the circumstances for the licence holder to comply with this Act\nor the regulations.\n(2) If the Regulator believes on reasonable grounds that:\n(a) one of the following kinds of persons is not complying with\nthis Act or the regulations in respect of a thing:\n(i) a person covered by a GMO licence;\n(ii) a person dealing with, or who has dealt with, a GMO\nspecified in an emergency dealing determination; and\n(b) either of the following applies:\n(i) it is necessary to exercise powers under this section in\norder to protect the health and safety of people or to\nprotect the environment;\n(ii) it is desirable in the public interest, having regard to the\nmatters specified in subsection (2A), for the Regulator\nto exercise powers under this section;\nthe Regulator may give directions to the person, by written notice,\nrequiring the person, within the time specified in the notice, to take\nsuch steps in relation to the thing as are reasonable in the\ncircumstances for the person to comply with this Act or the\nregulations.\n(2A) For the purposes of deciding under subparagraph (1)(b)(ii) or\n(2)(b)(ii) whether it is desirable to exercise powers under this"
    },
