    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-147",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "147 Injunctions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-147"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.121",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a person has engaged, is engaging, or is about to engage in any\nconduct that is or would be an offence against this Act or the\nregulations, the Federal Court of Australia (the Court) may, on the\napplication of the Regulator or any other aggrieved person, grant\nan injunction restraining the person from engaging in the conduct.\n(2) If:\n(a) a person has refused or failed, is refusing or failing, or is\nabout to refuse or fail, to do a thing; and\n(b) the refusal or failure is, or would be, an offence against this\nAct or the regulations;\nthe Court may, on the application of the Regulator or any other\naggrieved person, grant an injunction requiring the person to do the\nthing.\n(3) The power of the Court to grant an injunction may be exercised:\n(a) whether or not it appears to the Court that the person intends\nto engage, or to continue to engage, in conduct of that kind;\nand",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a person has engaged, is engaging, or is about to engage in any\nconduct that is or would be an offence against this Act or the\nregulations, the Federal Court of Australia (the Court) may, on the\napplication of the Regulator or any other aggrieved person, grant\nan injunction restraining the person from engaging in the conduct.\n(2) If:\n(a) a person has refused or failed, is refusing or failing, or is\nabout to refuse or fail, to do a thing; and\n(b) the refusal or failure is, or would be, an offence against this\nAct or the regulations;\nthe Court may, on the application of the Regulator or any other\naggrieved person, grant an injunction requiring the person to do the\nthing.\n(3) The power of the Court to grant an injunction may be exercised:\n(a) whether or not it appears to the Court that the person intends\nto engage, or to continue to engage, in conduct of that kind;\nand",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-147-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-147-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-147-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bb04629a99cb3b62bfae6c5d27420f881c9de49fca5a7282dc1d944356ac0b01"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-147",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "147 Injunctions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 121,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a person has engaged, is engaging, or is about to engage in any\nconduct that is or would be an offence against this Act or the\nregulations, the Federal Court of Australia (the Court) may, on the\napplication of the Regulator or any other aggrieved person, grant\nan injunction restraining the person from engaging in the conduct.\n(2) If:\n(a) a person has refused or failed, is refusing or failing, or is\nabout to refuse or fail, to do a thing; and\n(b) the refusal or failure is, or would be, an offence against this\nAct or the regulations;\nthe Court may, on the application of the Regulator or any other\naggrieved person, grant an injunction requiring the person to do the\nthing.\n(3) The power of the Court to grant an injunction may be exercised:\n(a) whether or not it appears to the Court that the person intends\nto engage, or to continue to engage, in conduct of that kind;\nand"
    },
