    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-148",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "148 Forfeiture",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-148"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.122",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a court:\n(a) convicts a person of an offence against this Act or the\nregulations; or\n(b) makes an order under section 19B of the Crimes Act 1914 in\nrespect of a person charged with an offence against this Act\nor the regulations;\nthe court may order forfeiture to the Commonwealth of any thing\nused or otherwise involved in the commission of the offence.\n(2) A thing ordered by a court to be forfeited under this section\nbecomes the property of the Commonwealth and may be sold or\notherwise dealt with in accordance with the directions of the\nRegulator.\n(3) Until the Regulator gives a direction, the thing must be kept in\nsuch custody as the Regulator directs.\n\n\nPowers of inspection  Part 11\nSimplified outline  Division 1\nSection 149\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a court:\n(a) convicts a person of an offence against this Act or the\nregulations; or\n(b) makes an order under section 19B of the Crimes Act 1914 in\nrespect of a person charged with an offence against this Act\nor the regulations;\nthe court may order forfeiture to the Commonwealth of any thing\nused or otherwise involved in the commission of the offence.\n(2) A thing ordered by a court to be forfeited under this section\nbecomes the property of the Commonwealth and may be sold or\notherwise dealt with in accordance with the directions of the\nRegulator.\n(3) Until the Regulator gives a direction, the thing must be kept in\nsuch custody as the Regulator directs.\n\n\nPowers of inspection  Part 11\nSimplified outline  Division 1\nSection 149\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-148-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-148-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-148-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b4c9376cfb38e60278d1a9f7b6a3b132981c005b88c84263b7aebcafd1c84056"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-148",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "148 Forfeiture",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 122,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a court:\n(a) convicts a person of an offence against this Act or the\nregulations; or\n(b) makes an order under section 19B of the Crimes Act 1914 in\nrespect of a person charged with an offence against this Act\nor the regulations;\nthe court may order forfeiture to the Commonwealth of any thing\nused or otherwise involved in the commission of the offence.\n(2) A thing ordered by a court to be forfeited under this section\nbecomes the property of the Commonwealth and may be sold or\notherwise dealt with in accordance with the directions of the\nRegulator.\n(3) Until the Regulator gives a direction, the thing must be kept in\nsuch custody as the Regulator directs.\n\n\nPowers of inspection  Part 11\nSimplified outline  Division 1\nSection 149\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024"
    },
