    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-152",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "152 Powers available to inspectors for monitoring compliance",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-152"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.125",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purpose of finding out whether this Act or the regulations\nhave been complied with, an inspector may:\n(a) enter any premises; and\n(b) exercise the monitoring powers set out in section 153.\n(2) An inspector is not authorised to enter premises under\nsubsection (1) unless:\n(a) the occupier of the premises has consented to the entry; or\n(b) the entry is made under a warrant under section 172; or\n(c) the occupier of the premises is a licence holder, or a person\ncovered by a licence, and the entry is at a reasonable time; or\n(d) the occupier of the premises is a person dealing with, or who\nhas dealt with, a GMO specified in an emergency dealing\ndetermination, and the entry is at a reasonable time.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purpose of finding out whether this Act or the regulations\nhave been complied with, an inspector may:\n(a) enter any premises; and\n(b) exercise the monitoring powers set out in section 153.\n(2) An inspector is not authorised to enter premises under\nsubsection (1) unless:\n(a) the occupier of the premises has consented to the entry; or\n(b) the entry is made under a warrant under section 172; or\n(c) the occupier of the premises is a licence holder, or a person\ncovered by a licence, and the entry is at a reasonable time; or\n(d) the occupier of the premises is a person dealing with, or who\nhas dealt with, a GMO specified in an emergency dealing\ndetermination, and the entry is at a reasonable time.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-152-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-152-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b0d8aa78408f216417a82ac107dbba38b0164fc2c4bde0ce8567eb3e1ed20ff1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-152",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "152 Powers available to inspectors for monitoring compliance",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 125,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purpose of finding out whether this Act or the regulations\nhave been complied with, an inspector may:\n(a) enter any premises; and\n(b) exercise the monitoring powers set out in section 153.\n(2) An inspector is not authorised to enter premises under\nsubsection (1) unless:\n(a) the occupier of the premises has consented to the entry; or\n(b) the entry is made under a warrant under section 172; or\n(c) the occupier of the premises is a licence holder, or a person\ncovered by a licence, and the entry is at a reasonable time; or\n(d) the occupier of the premises is a person dealing with, or who\nhas dealt with, a GMO specified in an emergency dealing\ndetermination, and the entry is at a reasonable time."
    },
