    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-153",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "153 Monitoring powers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-153"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.125",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The monitoring powers that an inspector may exercise under\nparagraph 152(1)(b) are as follows:\n(a) to search the premises and any thing on the premises;\n(b) to inspect, examine, take measurements of, conduct tests on,\nor take samples of, any thing on the premises that relates to a\nGMO;\n(c) to take photographs, make video or audio recordings or make\nsketches of the premises or any thing on the premises;\n(d) if the inspector was authorised to enter the premises by a\nwarrant under section 172—to require any person in or on the\npremises to:\n(i) answer any questions put by the inspector; and\n(ii) produce any book, record or document requested by the\ninspector;",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The monitoring powers that an inspector may exercise under\nparagraph 152(1)(b) are as follows:\n(a) to search the premises and any thing on the premises;\n(b) to inspect, examine, take measurements of, conduct tests on,\nor take samples of, any thing on the premises that relates to a\nGMO;\n(c) to take photographs, make video or audio recordings or make\nsketches of the premises or any thing on the premises;\n(d) if the inspector was authorised to enter the premises by a\nwarrant under section 172—to require any person in or on the\npremises to:\n(i) answer any questions put by the inspector; and\n(ii) produce any book, record or document requested by the\ninspector;",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-153-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-153-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e54c0101ff3a0f7315e1987fc7a92f49800b872de4794356e3bbc8ef90167112",
      "skos:note": "Inspector's powers to search and inspect premises"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-153",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "153 Monitoring powers",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 125,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The monitoring powers that an inspector may exercise under\nparagraph 152(1)(b) are as follows:\n(a) to search the premises and any thing on the premises;\n(b) to inspect, examine, take measurements of, conduct tests on,\nor take samples of, any thing on the premises that relates to a\nGMO;\n(c) to take photographs, make video or audio recordings or make\nsketches of the premises or any thing on the premises;\n(d) if the inspector was authorised to enter the premises by a\nwarrant under section 172—to require any person in or on the\npremises to:\n(i) answer any questions put by the inspector; and\n(ii) produce any book, record or document requested by the\ninspector;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-153-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
