      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Inspector is authorized",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Search is permitted"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-154",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "154 Searches and seizures related to offences",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-154"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.128",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if an inspector has reasonable grounds for\nsuspecting that there may be evidential material on any premises.\n(2) The inspector may:\n(a) enter the premises, with the consent of the occupier or under\na warrant issued under section 173; and\n(b) exercise the powers set out in subsection (3) and section 155;\nand\n(c) if the entry is under a warrant—seize the evidential material,\nif the inspector finds it on the premises.\n(3) If:\n(a) in the course of searching, in accordance with a warrant, for a\nparticular thing, an inspector finds another thing that the\ninspector believes on reasonable grounds to be evidential\nmaterial; and\n(b) the inspector believes, on reasonable grounds, that it is\nnecessary to seize that other thing in order to prevent its\nconcealment, loss or destruction, or its use in committing,\ncontinuing or repeating an offence against this Act or the\nregulations;\nthe warrant is taken to authorise the inspector to seize that other\nthing.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if an inspector has reasonable grounds for\nsuspecting that there may be evidential material on any premises.\n(2) The inspector may:\n(a) enter the premises, with the consent of the occupier or under\na warrant issued under section 173; and\n(b) exercise the powers set out in subsection (3) and section 155;\nand\n(c) if the entry is under a warrant—seize the evidential material,\nif the inspector finds it on the premises.\n(3) If:\n(a) in the course of searching, in accordance with a warrant, for a\nparticular thing, an inspector finds another thing that the\ninspector believes on reasonable grounds to be evidential\nmaterial; and\n(b) the inspector believes, on reasonable grounds, that it is\nnecessary to seize that other thing in order to prevent its\nconcealment, loss or destruction, or its use in committing,\ncontinuing or repeating an offence against this Act or the\nregulations;\nthe warrant is taken to authorise the inspector to seize that other\nthing.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-154-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-154-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-154-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "272b6770a864072236eb713905cf4e808cd64dbb9813ccbb66b300cdb94a3e38"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-154",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "154 Searches and seizures related to offences",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 128,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if an inspector has reasonable grounds for\nsuspecting that there may be evidential material on any premises.\n(2) The inspector may:\n(a) enter the premises, with the consent of the occupier or under\na warrant issued under section 173; and\n(b) exercise the powers set out in subsection (3) and section 155;\nand\n(c) if the entry is under a warrant—seize the evidential material,\nif the inspector finds it on the premises.\n(3) If:\n(a) in the course of searching, in accordance with a warrant, for a\nparticular thing, an inspector finds another thing that the\ninspector believes on reasonable grounds to be evidential\nmaterial; and\n(b) the inspector believes, on reasonable grounds, that it is\nnecessary to seize that other thing in order to prevent its\nconcealment, loss or destruction, or its use in committing,\ncontinuing or repeating an offence against this Act or the\nregulations;\nthe warrant is taken to authorise the inspector to seize that other\nthing."
    },
