    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-155",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "155 Offence-related powers of inspectors in relation to premises",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-155"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.128",
      "values:originalText": "The powers an inspector may exercise under paragraph 154(2)(b)\nare as follows:\n(a) to search the premises and any thing on the premises for the\nevidential material;\n(b) to inspect, examine, take measurements of, conduct tests on,\nor take samples of the evidential material;\n\n\nPowers of inspection  Part 11\nOffence-related powers  Division 4\nSection 156\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(c) to take photographs, make video or audio recordings or make\nsketches of the premises or the evidential material;\n(d) to take onto the premises such equipment and materials as the\ninspector requires for the purpose of exercising powers in\nrelation to the premises.",
      "skos:definition": "The powers an inspector may exercise under paragraph 154(2)(b)\nare as follows:\n(a) to search the premises and any thing on the premises for the\nevidential material;\n(b) to inspect, examine, take measurements of, conduct tests on,\nor take samples of the evidential material;\n\n\nPowers of inspection  Part 11\nOffence-related powers  Division 4\nSection 156\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(c) to take photographs, make video or audio recordings or make\nsketches of the premises or the evidential material;\n(d) to take onto the premises such equipment and materials as the\ninspector requires for the purpose of exercising powers in\nrelation to the premises.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-155-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-155-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3d400308fe0498dfba8e4b42659aef87cd742f58220a7ec66575872e1515305b",
      "skos:note": "Inspector's powers of search, inspection, and sampling"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-155",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "155 Offence-related powers of inspectors in relation to premises",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 128,
      "values:originalText": "The powers an inspector may exercise under paragraph 154(2)(b)\nare as follows:\n(a) to search the premises and any thing on the premises for the\nevidential material;\n(b) to inspect, examine, take measurements of, conduct tests on,\nor take samples of the evidential material;\n\n\nPowers of inspection  Part 11\nOffence-related powers  Division 4\nSection 156\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(c) to take photographs, make video or audio recordings or make\nsketches of the premises or the evidential material;\n(d) to take onto the premises such equipment and materials as the\ninspector requires for the purpose of exercising powers in\nrelation to the premises."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-155-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-155"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-155-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "hasPower",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Inspector has power to search premises",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-156",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "156 Use of equipment at premises",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-156"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.129",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The inspector may operate equipment at the premises to see\nwhether evidential material is accessible by doing so, if the\ninspector believes on reasonable grounds that the operation of the\nequipment can be carried out without damage to the equipment.\n(2) If the inspector, after operating the equipment, finds that evidential\nmaterial is accessible by doing so, the inspector may:\n(a) seize the equipment and any disk, tape or other associated\ndevice; or\n(b) if the material can, by using facilities at the premises, be put\nin documentary form—operate the facilities to put the\nmaterial in that form and seize the documents so produced; or\n(c) if the material can be transferred to a disk, tape or other\nstorage device that:\n(i) is brought to the premises; or\n(ii) is at the premises and the use of which for the purpose\nhas been agreed to in writing by the occupier of the\npremises;\noperate the equipment or other facilities to copy the material\nto the storage device and take the storage device from the\npremises.\n(3) An inspector may seize equipment under paragraph (2)(a) only if:\n(a) it is not practicable to put the material in documentary form\nas mentioned in paragraph (2)(b) or to copy the material as\nmentioned in paragraph (2)(c); or\n(b) possession by the occupier of the equipment could constitute\nan offence.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The inspector may operate equipment at the premises to see\nwhether evidential material is accessible by doing so, if the\ninspector believes on reasonable grounds that the operation of the\nequipment can be carried out without damage to the equipment.\n(2) If the inspector, after operating the equipment, finds that evidential\nmaterial is accessible by doing so, the inspector may:\n(a) seize the equipment and any disk, tape or other associated\ndevice; or\n(b) if the material can, by using facilities at the premises, be put\nin documentary form—operate the facilities to put the\nmaterial in that form and seize the documents so produced; or\n(c) if the material can be transferred to a disk, tape or other\nstorage device that:\n(i) is brought to the premises; or\n(ii) is at the premises and the use of which for the purpose\nhas been agreed to in writing by the occupier of the\npremises;\noperate the equipment or other facilities to copy the material\nto the storage device and take the storage device from the\npremises.\n(3) An inspector may seize equipment under paragraph (2)(a) only if:\n(a) it is not practicable to put the material in documentary form\nas mentioned in paragraph (2)(b) or to copy the material as\nmentioned in paragraph (2)(c); or\n(b) possession by the occupier of the equipment could constitute\nan offence.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-156-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-156-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-156-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "501d740a204e47fcb155337f1e9f60af415b2096dd89899e3282c1e0cceebd4c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-156",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "156 Use of equipment at premises",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 129,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The inspector may operate equipment at the premises to see\nwhether evidential material is accessible by doing so, if the\ninspector believes on reasonable grounds that the operation of the\nequipment can be carried out without damage to the equipment.\n(2) If the inspector, after operating the equipment, finds that evidential\nmaterial is accessible by doing so, the inspector may:\n(a) seize the equipment and any disk, tape or other associated\ndevice; or\n(b) if the material can, by using facilities at the premises, be put\nin documentary form—operate the facilities to put the\nmaterial in that form and seize the documents so produced; or\n(c) if the material can be transferred to a disk, tape or other\nstorage device that:\n(i) is brought to the premises; or\n(ii) is at the premises and the use of which for the purpose\nhas been agreed to in writing by the occupier of the\npremises;\noperate the equipment or other facilities to copy the material\nto the storage device and take the storage device from the\npremises.\n(3) An inspector may seize equipment under paragraph (2)(a) only if:\n(a) it is not practicable to put the material in documentary form\nas mentioned in paragraph (2)(b) or to copy the material as\nmentioned in paragraph (2)(c); or\n(b) possession by the occupier of the equipment could constitute\nan offence."
    },
