      "values:originalText": "(1) The inspector may operate equipment at the premises to see\nwhether evidential material is accessible by doing so, if the\ninspector believes on reasonable grounds that the operation of the\nequipment can be carried out without damage to the equipment.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The inspector may operate equipment at the premises to see\nwhether evidential material is accessible by doing so, if the\ninspector believes on reasonable grounds that the operation of the\nequipment can be carried out without damage to the equipment.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-156"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-156-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-156-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-156-ss-1-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "199c517a254b2a7f30666df705460fe0b727b8a306bb1bc22c1d8182b2c00f12",
      "skos:note": "Inspector may operate equipment to access evidential material."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-156-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "156(1) Use of equipment at premises",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 129,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The inspector may operate equipment at the premises to see\nwhether evidential material is accessible by doing so, if the\ninspector believes on reasonable grounds that the operation of the\nequipment can be carried out without damage to the equipment."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-156-ss-1-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
