      "cml:logicSummary": "Describes recognition of evidential material by inspector.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) If the inspector, after operating the equipment...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The inspector recognizes the evidential material if it is accessible."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-156-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "156(3) Use of equipment at premises",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-156-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.129",
      "values:originalText": "(3) An inspector may seize equipment under paragraph (2)(a) only if:\n(a) it is not practicable to put the material in documentary form\nas mentioned in paragraph (2)(b) or to copy the material as\nmentioned in paragraph (2)(c); or\n(b) possession by the occupier of the equipment could constitute\nan offence.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) An inspector may seize equipment under paragraph (2)(a) only if:\n(a) it is not practicable to put the material in documentary form\nas mentioned in paragraph (2)(b) or to copy the material as\nmentioned in paragraph (2)(c); or\n(b) possession by the occupier of the equipment could constitute\nan offence.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-156"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-156-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-156-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a20fa67ce36b0e9329c0c49cff0d3eccd77db42b990a6e71b5aede01d62b96a8",
      "skos:note": "Seizure of equipment under certain conditions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-156-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "156(3) Use of equipment at premises",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 129,
      "values:originalText": "(3) An inspector may seize equipment under paragraph (2)(a) only if:\n(a) it is not practicable to put the material in documentary form\nas mentioned in paragraph (2)(b) or to copy the material as\nmentioned in paragraph (2)(c); or\n(b) possession by the occupier of the equipment could constitute\nan offence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-156-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-156-ss-3"
