      "values:originalText": "(1) If an inspector believes on reasonable grounds that:\n(a) information relevant to determining whether there has been\ncompliance with this Act or the regulations, or evidential\nmaterial, may be accessible by operating a thing at particular\npremises; and\n(b) expert assistance is required to operate the thing; and\n(c) if he or she does not take action under this subsection, the\ninformation or material may be destroyed, altered or\notherwise interfered with;\nhe or she may do whatever is necessary to secure the thing,\nwhether by locking it up, placing a guard or otherwise."
