    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-158-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "158(2) Powers available to inspectors for dealing with dangerous",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-158-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.132",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The inspector may do any of the following:\n(a) enter the premises;\n(b) search the premises for the thing;\n(c) secure the thing, if the inspector finds it on the premises,\nuntil a warrant is obtained to seize the thing;\n(d) if the inspector has reasonable grounds for suspecting that a\nperson has not complied with this Act or the regulations in\nrespect of the thing—require the person to take such steps as\nthe inspector considers necessary for the person to comply\nwith this Act or the regulations;\n(e) take such steps, or arrange for such steps to be taken, in\nrelation to the thing as the inspector considers appropriate.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The inspector may do any of the following:\n(a) enter the premises;\n(b) search the premises for the thing;\n(c) secure the thing, if the inspector finds it on the premises,\nuntil a warrant is obtained to seize the thing;\n(d) if the inspector has reasonable grounds for suspecting that a\nperson has not complied with this Act or the regulations in\nrespect of the thing—require the person to take such steps as\nthe inspector considers necessary for the person to comply\nwith this Act or the regulations;\n(e) take such steps, or arrange for such steps to be taken, in\nrelation to the thing as the inspector considers appropriate.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-158"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-158-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-158-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-158-ss-2-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-158-ss-2-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-158-ss-2-logic-deontic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "be4491cba971a2815190124395159f7f553bbf0cbaf4c268e83f9675c7d9ba33",
      "skos:note": "Inspector's powers to deal with dangerous things"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-158-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "158(2) Powers available to inspectors for dealing with dangerous",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 132,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The inspector may do any of the following:\n(a) enter the premises;\n(b) search the premises for the thing;\n(c) secure the thing, if the inspector finds it on the premises,\nuntil a warrant is obtained to seize the thing;\n(d) if the inspector has reasonable grounds for suspecting that a\nperson has not complied with this Act or the regulations in\nrespect of the thing—require the person to take such steps as\nthe inspector considers necessary for the person to comply\nwith this Act or the regulations;\n(e) take such steps, or arrange for such steps to be taken, in\nrelation to the thing as the inspector considers appropriate."
    },
    {
