    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-158-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "158(4) Powers available to inspectors for dealing with dangerous",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-158-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.132",
      "values:originalText": "(4) If the Regulator incurs costs because of steps reasonably taken or\narranged to be taken by an inspector under paragraph (2)(e), the\nperson is liable to pay to the Commonwealth an amount equal to\nthe costs, and the amount may be recovered by the Commonwealth\nas a debt due to the Commonwealth in a court of competent\njurisdiction.\n\n\nPowers of inspection  Part 11\nObligations and incidental powers of inspectors  Division 7\nSection 159\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024",
      "skos:definition": "(4) If the Regulator incurs costs because of steps reasonably taken or\narranged to be taken by an inspector under paragraph (2)(e), the\nperson is liable to pay to the Commonwealth an amount equal to\nthe costs, and the amount may be recovered by the Commonwealth\nas a debt due to the Commonwealth in a court of competent\njurisdiction.\n\n\nPowers of inspection  Part 11\nObligations and incidental powers of inspectors  Division 7\nSection 159\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-158"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-158-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-158-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a2e1808b14c2beccb5e73402ff4b50bc0e721b88e00496ba60e30d0de28a8bcd",
      "skos:note": "Person liable for costs incurred by Commonwealth due to inspector's actions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-158-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "158(4) Powers available to inspectors for dealing with dangerous",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 132,
      "values:originalText": "(4) If the Regulator incurs costs because of steps reasonably taken or\narranged to be taken by an inspector under paragraph (2)(e), the\nperson is liable to pay to the Commonwealth an amount equal to\nthe costs, and the amount may be recovered by the Commonwealth\nas a debt due to the Commonwealth in a court of competent\njurisdiction.\n\n\nPowers of inspection  Part 11\nObligations and incidental powers of inspectors  Division 7\nSection 159\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024"
    },
    {
