    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-163",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "163 Compensation for damage",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-163"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.134",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The owner of a thing is entitled to compensation for damage to the\nthing if:\n(a) the damage was caused to the thing as a result of it being\noperated as mentioned in this Part; and\n(b) the damage was caused as a result of:\n(i) insufficient care being exercised in selecting the person\nwho was to operate the thing; or\n(ii) insufficient care being exercised by the person operating\nthe thing.\n(2) Compensation is payable out of money appropriated by the\nParliament.\n(3) In determining the amount of compensation payable, regard is to\nbe had to whether the occupier of the premises and his or her\nemployees and agents, if they were available at the time, had\nprovided any warning or guidance as to the operation of the thing\nthat was appropriate in the circumstances.\n\n\nPowers of inspection  Part 11\nPower to search goods, baggage etc.  Division 8\nSection 164\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The owner of a thing is entitled to compensation for damage to the\nthing if:\n(a) the damage was caused to the thing as a result of it being\noperated as mentioned in this Part; and\n(b) the damage was caused as a result of:\n(i) insufficient care being exercised in selecting the person\nwho was to operate the thing; or\n(ii) insufficient care being exercised by the person operating\nthe thing.\n(2) Compensation is payable out of money appropriated by the\nParliament.\n(3) In determining the amount of compensation payable, regard is to\nbe had to whether the occupier of the premises and his or her\nemployees and agents, if they were available at the time, had\nprovided any warning or guidance as to the operation of the thing\nthat was appropriate in the circumstances.\n\n\nPowers of inspection  Part 11\nPower to search goods, baggage etc.  Division 8\nSection 164\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-163-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-163-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-163-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c327bf1c055ecf4c23553f61242913830cc58ebed5b39a452e5cf28999fd845a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-163",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "163 Compensation for damage",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 134,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The owner of a thing is entitled to compensation for damage to the\nthing if:\n(a) the damage was caused to the thing as a result of it being\noperated as mentioned in this Part; and\n(b) the damage was caused as a result of:\n(i) insufficient care being exercised in selecting the person\nwho was to operate the thing; or\n(ii) insufficient care being exercised by the person operating\nthe thing.\n(2) Compensation is payable out of money appropriated by the\nParliament.\n(3) In determining the amount of compensation payable, regard is to\nbe had to whether the occupier of the premises and his or her\nemployees and agents, if they were available at the time, had\nprovided any warning or guidance as to the operation of the thing\nthat was appropriate in the circumstances.\n\n\nPowers of inspection  Part 11\nPower to search goods, baggage etc.  Division 8\nSection 164\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024"
    },
