    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-166",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "166 Copies of seized things to be provided",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-166"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.136",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), if an inspector seizes, under a warrant\nrelating to premises:\n(a) a document, film, computer file or other thing that can be\nreadily copied; or\n(b) a storage device, the information in which can be readily\ncopied;\nthe inspector must, if requested to do so by the occupier of the\npremises, or another person who apparently represents the occupier\nand who is present when the warrant is executed, give a copy of the\nthing or the information to that person as soon as practicable after\nthe seizure.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n(a) the thing that has been seized was seized under\nparagraph 156(2)(b) or (c); or\n(b) possession by the occupier of the document, film, computer\nfile, thing or information could constitute an offence.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), if an inspector seizes, under a warrant\nrelating to premises:\n(a) a document, film, computer file or other thing that can be\nreadily copied; or\n(b) a storage device, the information in which can be readily\ncopied;\nthe inspector must, if requested to do so by the occupier of the\npremises, or another person who apparently represents the occupier\nand who is present when the warrant is executed, give a copy of the\nthing or the information to that person as soon as practicable after\nthe seizure.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n(a) the thing that has been seized was seized under\nparagraph 156(2)(b) or (c); or\n(b) possession by the occupier of the document, film, computer\nfile, thing or information could constitute an offence.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-166-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-166-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "72c332689e56c4fd802dbb7250e6472cb44a5de1b546c25014eb1b9a71712db2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-166",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "166 Copies of seized things to be provided",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 136,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), if an inspector seizes, under a warrant\nrelating to premises:\n(a) a document, film, computer file or other thing that can be\nreadily copied; or\n(b) a storage device, the information in which can be readily\ncopied;\nthe inspector must, if requested to do so by the occupier of the\npremises, or another person who apparently represents the occupier\nand who is present when the warrant is executed, give a copy of the\nthing or the information to that person as soon as practicable after\nthe seizure.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n(a) the thing that has been seized was seized under\nparagraph 156(2)(b) or (c); or\n(b) possession by the occupier of the document, film, computer\nfile, thing or information could constitute an offence."
    },
