      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.137",
      "values:originalText": "(2) At the end of the 60 days specified in subsection (1), an inspector\nmust take reasonable steps to return the thing to the person from\nwhom it was seized, unless:\n(a) proceedings in respect of which the thing may afford\nevidence were instituted before the end of the 60 days and\nhave not been completed (including an appeal to a court in\nrelation to those proceedings); or\n(b) an inspector may retain the thing because of an order under\nsection 170; or\n(c) to return the thing could cause an imminent risk of death,\nserious illness, serious injury or serious damage to the\nenvironment; or\n(d) an inspector is otherwise authorised (by a law, or an order of\na court, of the Commonwealth or of a State) to retain, destroy\nor dispose of the thing.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) At the end of the 60 days specified in subsection (1), an inspector\nmust take reasonable steps to return the thing to the person from\nwhom it was seized, unless:\n(a) proceedings in respect of which the thing may afford\nevidence were instituted before the end of the 60 days and\nhave not been completed (including an appeal to a court in\nrelation to those proceedings); or\n(b) an inspector may retain the thing because of an order under\nsection 170; or\n(c) to return the thing could cause an imminent risk of death,\nserious illness, serious injury or serious damage to the\nenvironment; or\n(d) an inspector is otherwise authorised (by a law, or an order of\na court, of the Commonwealth or of a State) to retain, destroy\nor dispose of the thing.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-169"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-169-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-169-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "26872d1dac36a49c50cc7680b3bcd3c5a0edd1878851f463cbbdf47d262539fb",
      "skos:note": "Return seized thing within 60 days unless certain conditions apply."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-169-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "169(2) Retention of seized things",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 137,
      "values:originalText": "(2) At the end of the 60 days specified in subsection (1), an inspector\nmust take reasonable steps to return the thing to the person from\nwhom it was seized, unless:\n(a) proceedings in respect of which the thing may afford\nevidence were instituted before the end of the 60 days and\nhave not been completed (including an appeal to a court in\nrelation to those proceedings); or\n(b) an inspector may retain the thing because of an order under\nsection 170; or\n(c) to return the thing could cause an imminent risk of death,\nserious illness, serious injury or serious damage to the\nenvironment; or\n(d) an inspector is otherwise authorised (by a law, or an order of\na court, of the Commonwealth or of a State) to retain, destroy\nor dispose of the thing."
    },
