      "cml:conclusionText": "Inspector retains thing due to AI-assisted magistrate's order."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-170-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "170(3) Magistrate may permit a thing to be retained",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-170-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.138",
      "values:originalText": "(3) Before making the application, the inspector must:\n(a) take reasonable steps to discover who has an interest in the\nretention of the thing; and\n(b) if it is practicable to do so, notify each person whom the\ninspector believes to have such an interest of the proposed\napplication.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) Before making the application, the inspector must:\n(a) take reasonable steps to discover who has an interest in the\nretention of the thing; and\n(b) if it is practicable to do so, notify each person whom the\ninspector believes to have such an interest of the proposed\napplication.",
