        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-172-ss-4-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-172-ss-4-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-172-ss-4-logic-deontic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9127784e354b98a6224f6cef07bc01807dd66d679410b41e4418dae5a41c502a",
      "skos:note": "Warrant must authorise entry and exercise powers",
      "dc:description": "(a) authorise one or more inspectors, (b) state purpose for which warrant is issued"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-172-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "172(4) Monitoring warrants",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 140,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The warrant must:\n(a) authorise one or more inspectors (whether or not named in\nthe warrant), with such assistance and by such force as is\nnecessary and reasonable:\n(i) to enter the premises; and\n(ii) to exercise the powers set out in section 153 in relation\nto the premises; and\n(b) state whether the entry is authorised to be made at any time\nof the day or night or during specified hours of the day or\nnight; and\n(c) specify the day (not more than 6 months after the issue of the\nwarrant) on which the warrant ceases to have effect; and\n(d) state the purpose for which the warrant is issued."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-172-ss-4-norm",
