    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-173-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "173(4) Offence-related warrants",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-173-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.140",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The warrant must:\n(a) name one or more inspectors; and\n(b) authorise the inspectors so named, with such assistance and\nby such force as is necessary and reasonable:\n(i) to enter the premises; and\n(ii) to exercise the powers set out in subsection 154(3) and\nsection 155; and\n(iii) to seize the evidential material; and\n(c) state whether the entry is authorised to be made at any time\nof the day or night or during specified hours of the day or\nnight; and\n(d) specify the day (not more than one week after the issue of the\nwarrant) on which the warrant ceases to have effect; and\n(e) state the purpose for which the warrant is issued.\n174  Offence-related warrants by telephone, telex, fax etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The warrant must:\n(a) name one or more inspectors; and\n(b) authorise the inspectors so named, with such assistance and\nby such force as is necessary and reasonable:\n(i) to enter the premises; and\n(ii) to exercise the powers set out in subsection 154(3) and\nsection 155; and\n(iii) to seize the evidential material; and\n(c) state whether the entry is authorised to be made at any time\nof the day or night or during specified hours of the day or\nnight; and\n(d) specify the day (not more than one week after the issue of the\nwarrant) on which the warrant ceases to have effect; and\n(e) state the purpose for which the warrant is issued.\n174  Offence-related warrants by telephone, telex, fax etc.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-173"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-173-ss-4-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ad439b3390e540153dcb45584a9910856969a2f0f1f402988161e8d286566f24",
      "skos:note": "Warrant requirements for inspectors",
      "dc:description": "(a) name one or more inspectors; (b) authorise the inspectors so named, with such assistance and by such force as is necessary and reasonable; (c) state whether the entry is authorised to be made at any time of the day or night or during specified hours of the day or night; (d) specify the day on which the warrant ceases to have effect; (e) state the purpose for which the warrant is issued."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-173-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "173(4) Offence-related warrants",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 140,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The warrant must:\n(a) name one or more inspectors; and\n(b) authorise the inspectors so named, with such assistance and\nby such force as is necessary and reasonable:\n(i) to enter the premises; and\n(ii) to exercise the powers set out in subsection 154(3) and\nsection 155; and\n(iii) to seize the evidential material; and\n(c) state whether the entry is authorised to be made at any time\nof the day or night or during specified hours of the day or\nnight; and\n(d) specify the day (not more than one week after the issue of the\nwarrant) on which the warrant ceases to have effect; and\n(e) state the purpose for which the warrant is issued.\n174  Offence-related warrants by telephone, telex, fax etc."
    },
