    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-181",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "181 Internal review",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-181"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.149",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An eligible person in relation to a reviewable decision (other than a\ndecision made by the Regulator personally) may apply in writing to\nthe Regulator for review (internal review) of the decision.\n(2) An application for internal review must be made within 30 days\nafter the day on which the decision first came to the notice of the\napplicant, or within such period (if any) as the Regulator, either\nbefore or after the end of that period, allows.\n(3) The Regulator must, on receiving an application, review the\nreviewable decision personally.\n(4) The Regulator may:\n(a) make a decision affirming, varying or revoking the\nreviewable decision; and\n(b) if the Regulator revokes the decision, make such other\ndecision as the Regulator thinks appropriate.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An eligible person in relation to a reviewable decision (other than a\ndecision made by the Regulator personally) may apply in writing to\nthe Regulator for review (internal review) of the decision.\n(2) An application for internal review must be made within 30 days\nafter the day on which the decision first came to the notice of the\napplicant, or within such period (if any) as the Regulator, either\nbefore or after the end of that period, allows.\n(3) The Regulator must, on receiving an application, review the\nreviewable decision personally.\n(4) The Regulator may:\n(a) make a decision affirming, varying or revoking the\nreviewable decision; and\n(b) if the Regulator revokes the decision, make such other\ndecision as the Regulator thinks appropriate.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-181-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-181-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-181-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-181-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "826a3377e39facbd9f749e9e86d868521c254d422cd5bd3837f83ffd73d0a390"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-181",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "181 Internal review",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 149,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An eligible person in relation to a reviewable decision (other than a\ndecision made by the Regulator personally) may apply in writing to\nthe Regulator for review (internal review) of the decision.\n(2) An application for internal review must be made within 30 days\nafter the day on which the decision first came to the notice of the\napplicant, or within such period (if any) as the Regulator, either\nbefore or after the end of that period, allows.\n(3) The Regulator must, on receiving an application, review the\nreviewable decision personally.\n(4) The Regulator may:\n(a) make a decision affirming, varying or revoking the\nreviewable decision; and\n(b) if the Regulator revokes the decision, make such other\ndecision as the Regulator thinks appropriate."
    },
