    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-183a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "183A Extended standing for judicial review",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-183a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.150",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section extends (and does not limit) the meaning of the term\nperson aggrieved in the Administrative Decisions (Judicial\nReview) Act 1977 for the purposes of the application of that Act in\nrelation to:\n(a) a decision made under this Act or the regulations; or\n(b) a failure to make a decision under this Act or the regulations;\nor\n(c) conduct engaged in for the purpose of making a decision\nunder this Act or the regulations.\n(2) A State is taken to be a person aggrieved by the decision, failure or\nconduct.\n(3) A term (except person aggrieved) used in this section and in the\nAdministrative Decisions (Judicial Review) Act 1977 has the same\nmeaning in this section as it has in that Act.\n\n\nMiscellaneous  Part 12\nConfidential commercial information  Division 3\nSection 184\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section extends (and does not limit) the meaning of the term\nperson aggrieved in the Administrative Decisions (Judicial\nReview) Act 1977 for the purposes of the application of that Act in\nrelation to:\n(a) a decision made under this Act or the regulations; or\n(b) a failure to make a decision under this Act or the regulations;\nor\n(c) conduct engaged in for the purpose of making a decision\nunder this Act or the regulations.\n(2) A State is taken to be a person aggrieved by the decision, failure or\nconduct.\n(3) A term (except person aggrieved) used in this section and in the\nAdministrative Decisions (Judicial Review) Act 1977 has the same\nmeaning in this section as it has in that Act.\n\n\nMiscellaneous  Part 12\nConfidential commercial information  Division 3\nSection 184\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-183a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-183a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-183a-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "30b63cbe8f10d04e8c064e2e2d3e9bc68db52a882366ae80a177bc3d13ad14fd"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-183a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "183A Extended standing for judicial review",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 150,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section extends (and does not limit) the meaning of the term\nperson aggrieved in the Administrative Decisions (Judicial\nReview) Act 1977 for the purposes of the application of that Act in\nrelation to:\n(a) a decision made under this Act or the regulations; or\n(b) a failure to make a decision under this Act or the regulations;\nor\n(c) conduct engaged in for the purpose of making a decision\nunder this Act or the regulations.\n(2) A State is taken to be a person aggrieved by the decision, failure or\nconduct.\n(3) A term (except person aggrieved) used in this section and in the\nAdministrative Decisions (Judicial Review) Act 1977 has the same\nmeaning in this section as it has in that Act.\n\n\nMiscellaneous  Part 12\nConfidential commercial information  Division 3\nSection 184\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024"
    },
