    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-186",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "186 Revocation of declaration",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-186"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.153",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Regulator may, by written notice given to the applicant,\nrevoke a declaration under section 185 if the Regulator is satisfied:\n(a) that the information concerned no longer satisfies\nparagraph 185(1)(a), (b) or (c); or\n(b) that the public interest in disclosure of the information\noutweighs the prejudice that disclosure would cause to any\nperson.\n(2) A revocation by the Regulator under subsection (1) does not take\neffect until any review rights under section 181 or 183 in relation\nto the revocation are exhausted.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Regulator may, by written notice given to the applicant,\nrevoke a declaration under section 185 if the Regulator is satisfied:\n(a) that the information concerned no longer satisfies\nparagraph 185(1)(a), (b) or (c); or\n(b) that the public interest in disclosure of the information\noutweighs the prejudice that disclosure would cause to any\nperson.\n(2) A revocation by the Regulator under subsection (1) does not take\neffect until any review rights under section 181 or 183 in relation\nto the revocation are exhausted.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-186-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-186-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1688320290c49c27f4bea082e53ae02f9abbc574ddfa9af48802b1c9090170dc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-186",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "186 Revocation of declaration",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 153,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Regulator may, by written notice given to the applicant,\nrevoke a declaration under section 185 if the Regulator is satisfied:\n(a) that the information concerned no longer satisfies\nparagraph 185(1)(a), (b) or (c); or\n(b) that the public interest in disclosure of the information\noutweighs the prejudice that disclosure would cause to any\nperson.\n(2) A revocation by the Regulator under subsection (1) does not take\neffect until any review rights under section 181 or 183 in relation\nto the revocation are exhausted."
    },
    {
