      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits disclosure of confidential commercial information.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(1) A person who...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "must not disclose the information except..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-187-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Temporal Interval",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Defines the temporal interval for which confidentiality is required.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(c) knows that the information is confidential commercial information;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "and (d) to any of the following in the course of carrying out duties or functions under this Act or under a corresponding State law:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-187-logic-diffusion-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Diffusion"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Diffuse",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Diffuses the requirement that confidential commercial information must not be disclosed.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::diffusion",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(i) the Commonwealth or a Commonwealth authority;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "or (ii) a State agency;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-187-logic-cogai-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:CogAI"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Recognize",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Recognizes the artificial intelligence system that can process confidential commercial information.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(iii) an artificial intelligence system;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "or (iv) a natural person or legal person;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-187-logic-shacl-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:SHACL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Validate",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Validates the shape of the data that contains confidential commercial information.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::shacl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(v) a data set containing confidential commercial information;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "or (vi) a natural person or legal person;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-188",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "188 Conduct by directors, employees and agents",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-188"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.156",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If, in proceedings for an offence against this Act or the regulations,\nor an ancillary offence in relation to this Act or the regulations, it is\nnecessary to establish the state of mind of a body corporate in\nrelation to particular conduct, it is sufficient to show:\n(a) that the conduct was engaged in by a director, employee or\nagent of the body corporate within the scope of his or her\nactual or apparent authority; and\n(b) that the director, employee or agent had the state of mind.\n(2) Any conduct engaged in on behalf of a body corporate by a\ndirector, employee or agent of the body corporate within the scope\nof his or her actual or apparent authority is taken, for the purposes\nof a prosecution for:\n(a) an offence against this Act or the regulations; or\n(b) an ancillary offence relating to this Act or the regulations;\nto have been engaged in also by the body corporate, unless the\nbody corporate establishes that the body corporate took reasonable\nprecautions and exercised due diligence to avoid the conduct.\n(3) If, in proceedings for an ancillary offence relating to this Act or the\nregulations, it is necessary to establish the state of mind of a person\nother than a body corporate in relation to particular conduct, it is\nsufficient to show:\n(a) that the conduct was engaged in by an employee or agent of\nthe person within the scope of his or her actual or apparent\nauthority; and\n(b) that the employee or agent had the state of mind.\n(4) Any conduct engaged in on behalf of a person (the first person),\nother than a body corporate, by an employee or agent of the first\nperson, within the scope of the actual or apparent authority of the\nemployee or agent is taken, for the purposes of a prosecution for:\n(a) an offence against this Act or the regulations; or\n\n\nMiscellaneous  Part 12\nConduct by directors, employees and agents  Division 4\nSection 189\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(b) an ancillary offence relating to this Act or the regulations;\nto have been engaged in also by the first person unless the first\nperson establishes that he or she took reasonable precautions and\nexercised due diligence to avoid the conduct.\n(5) If:\n(a) a person other than a body corporate is convicted of an\noffence; and\n(b) the person would not have been convicted of the offence if\nsubsections (3) and (4) had not been enacted;\nthe person is not liable to be punished by imprisonment for that\noffence.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If, in proceedings for an offence against this Act or the regulations,\nor an ancillary offence in relation to this Act or the regulations, it is\nnecessary to establish the state of mind of a body corporate in\nrelation to particular conduct, it is sufficient to show:\n(a) that the conduct was engaged in by a director, employee or\nagent of the body corporate within the scope of his or her\nactual or apparent authority; and\n(b) that the director, employee or agent had the state of mind.\n(2) Any conduct engaged in on behalf of a body corporate by a\ndirector, employee or agent of the body corporate within the scope\nof his or her actual or apparent authority is taken, for the purposes\nof a prosecution for:\n(a) an offence against this Act or the regulations; or\n(b) an ancillary offence relating to this Act or the regulations;\nto have been engaged in also by the body corporate, unless the\nbody corporate establishes that the body corporate took reasonable\nprecautions and exercised due diligence to avoid the conduct.\n(3) If, in proceedings for an ancillary offence relating to this Act or the\nregulations, it is necessary to establish the state of mind of a person\nother than a body corporate in relation to particular conduct, it is\nsufficient to show:\n(a) that the conduct was engaged in by an employee or agent of\nthe person within the scope of his or her actual or apparent\nauthority; and\n(b) that the employee or agent had the state of mind.\n(4) Any conduct engaged in on behalf of a person (the first person),\nother than a body corporate, by an employee or agent of the first\nperson, within the scope of the actual or apparent authority of the\nemployee or agent is taken, for the purposes of a prosecution for:\n(a) an offence against this Act or the regulations; or\n\n\nMiscellaneous  Part 12\nConduct by directors, employees and agents  Division 4\nSection 189\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(b) an ancillary offence relating to this Act or the regulations;\nto have ",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-188-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-188-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-188-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-188-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-188-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "86ccc2089944d232d315e38c00d619ada82193f9fe4992b5bfcbf36a6dded76e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-188",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "188 Conduct by directors, employees and agents",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 156,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If, in proceedings for an offence against this Act or the regulations,\nor an ancillary offence in relation to this Act or the regulations, it is\nnecessary to establish the state of mind of a body corporate in\nrelation to particular conduct, it is sufficient to show:\n(a) that the conduct was engaged in by a director, employee or\nagent of the body corporate within the scope of his or her\nactual or apparent authority; and\n(b) that the director, employee or agent had the state of mind.\n(2) Any conduct engaged in on behalf of a body corporate by a\ndirector, employee or agent of the body corporate within the scope\nof his or her actual or apparent authority is taken, for the purposes\nof a prosecution for:\n(a) an offence against this Act or the regulations; or\n(b) an ancillary offence relating to this Act or the regulations;\nto have been engaged in also by the body corporate, unless the\nbody corporate establishes that the body corporate took reasonable\nprecautions and exercised due diligence to avoid the conduct.\n(3) If, in proceedings for an ancillary offence relating to this Act or the\nregulations, it is necessary to establish the state of mind of a person\nother than a body corporate in relation to particular conduct, it is\nsufficient to show:\n(a) that the conduct was engaged in by an employee or agent of\nthe person within the scope of his or her actual or apparent\nauthority; and\n(b) that the employee or agent had the state of mind.\n(4) Any conduct engaged in on behalf of a person (the first person),\nother than a body corporate, by an employee or agent of the first\nperson, within the scope of the actual or apparent authority of the\nemployee or agent is taken, for the purposes of a prosecution for:\n(a) an offence against this Act or the regulations; or\n\n\nMiscellaneous  Part 12\nConduct by directors, employees and agents  Division 4\nSection 189\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(b) an ancillary offence relating to this Act or the regulations;\nto have been engaged in also by the first person unless the first\nperson establishes that he or she took reasonable precautions and\nexercised due diligence to avoid the conduct.\n(5) If:\n(a) a person other than a body corporate is convicted of an\noffence; and\n(b) the person would not have been convicted of the offence if\nsubsections (3) and (4) had not been enacted;\nthe person is not liable to be punished by imprisonment for that\noffence."
    },
    {
