      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-192-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "forbid",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibition on providing false or misleading information",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-192a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "192A Interference with dealings with GMOs",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-192a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.160",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person engages in conduct; and\n(b) the conduct:\n(i) results in damage to, destruction of, or interference\nwith, premises at which dealings with GMOs are being\nundertaken; or\n\n\nMiscellaneous  Part 12\nOther  Division 6\nSection 193\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(ii) involves damaging, destroying, or interfering with, a\nthing at, or removing a thing from, such premises; and\n(c) the owner or occupier of the premises, or the owner of the\nthing (as the case requires), has not consented to the conduct;\nand\n(d) in engaging in the conduct, the person intends to prevent or\nhinder authorised GMO dealings that are being undertaken at\nthe premises or facility; and\n(e) the person knows, or is reckless as to, the matters mentioned\nin paragraphs (b) and (c).\nMaximum penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years or 120 penalty units.\nNote:\nChapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of\ncriminal responsibility.\n(2) In this section:\nauthorised GMO dealings, in relation to premises or a facility,\nmeans dealings with GMOs being undertaken at the premises or\nfacility:\n(a) that are authorised to be undertaken at the premises or facility\nby a GMO licence; or\n(aa) that are specified in an emergency dealing determination and\nare not prohibited from being undertaken at the premises or\nfacility by a condition of the determination; or\n(b) that are notifiable low risk dealings; or\n(c) that are exempt dealings; or\n(d) that are dealings included on the GMO Register.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person engages in conduct; and\n(b) the conduct:\n(i) results in damage to, destruction of, or interference\nwith, premises at which dealings with GMOs are being\nundertaken; or\n\n\nMiscellaneous  Part 12\nOther  Division 6\nSection 193\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(ii) involves damaging, destroying, or interfering with, a\nthing at, or removing a thing from, such premises; and\n(c) the owner or occupier of the premises, or the owner of the\nthing (as the case requires), has not consented to the conduct;\nand\n(d) in engaging in the conduct, the person intends to prevent or\nhinder authorised GMO dealings that are being undertaken at\nthe premises or facility; and\n(e) the person knows, or is reckless as to, the matters mentioned\nin paragraphs (b) and (c).\nMaximum penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years or 120 penalty units.\nNote:\nChapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of\ncriminal responsibility.\n(2) In this section:\nauthorised GMO dealings, in relation to premises or a facility,\nmeans dealings with GMOs being undertaken at the premises or\nfacility:\n(a) that are authorised to be undertaken at the premises or facility\nby a GMO licence; or\n(aa) that are specified in an emergency dealing determination and\nare not prohibited from being undertaken at the premises or\nfacility by a condition of the determination; or\n(b) that are notifiable low risk dealings; or\n(c) that are exempt dealings; or\n(d) that are dealings included on the GMO Register.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-192a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-192a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "11c131033d0311eb030daebcd7f659aa87a62f79e69cc442d9f528bdedd222b3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-act-2000#sec-192a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "192A Interference with dealings with GMOs",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 160,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person engages in conduct; and\n(b) the conduct:\n(i) results in damage to, destruction of, or interference\nwith, premises at which dealings with GMOs are being\nundertaken; or\n\n\nMiscellaneous  Part 12\nOther  Division 6\nSection 193\nGene Technology Act 2000\nCompilation date: 14/10/2024\n(ii) involves damaging, destroying, or interfering with, a\nthing at, or removing a thing from, such premises; and\n(c) the owner or occupier of the premises, or the owner of the\nthing (as the case requires), has not consented to the conduct;\nand\n(d) in engaging in the conduct, the person intends to prevent or\nhinder authorised GMO dealings that are being undertaken at\nthe premises or facility; and\n(e) the person knows, or is reckless as to, the matters mentioned\nin paragraphs (b) and (c).\nMaximum penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years or 120 penalty units.\nNote:\nChapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of\ncriminal responsibility.\n(2) In this section:\nauthorised GMO dealings, in relation to premises or a facility,\nmeans dealings with GMOs being undertaken at the premises or\nfacility:\n(a) that are authorised to be undertaken at the premises or facility\nby a GMO licence; or\n(aa) that are specified in an emergency dealing determination and\nare not prohibited from being undertaken at the premises or\nfacility by a condition of the determination; or\n(b) that are notifiable low risk dealings; or\n(c) that are exempt dealings; or\n(d) that are dealings included on the GMO Register."
    },
